"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/ff37212a8e2155dbb5d31a5025a19a724c57dc27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T14:55:56Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T14:55:56Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"message":"fix(auth): real Argon2id + correct endpoints + Android client parity\n\nOUT OF SCOPE for the change add-admin-ui-index-html but discovered\nduring its testing. The auth flow was five coupled bugs, all in\nsrc/lib/fmd-auth.ts:\n\n  A. deriveKey did PBKDF2, not Argon2id. Wrong KDF entirely.\n  B. base64ToBytes rejected URL-safe Base64. FMD servers return\n     salts in URL-safe form (`-_ alphabet, no padding`).\n  C. Endpoint paths were wrong. The old code targeted the\n     pre-v0.14 paths; the real server uses POST /salt,\n     PUT /requestAccess, POST /key.\n  D. The two-step client KDF was missing. The client must run\n     Argon2id with parameters M=128 MiB, T=1, P=4, len=32 over\n     the password prefixed with ''context:loginAuthentication'',\n     then send the full PHC string (not just the hash portion) to\n     PUT /requestAccess. The server-side SHA-512 of the PHC\n     string is what authenticates.\n  E. getPrivateKey was GET with IDT header. The real endpoint is\n     POST /key with {IDT: <accessToken>} in the body.\n\nThe Argon2id parameters and the context string were verified by\nreading /Users/tschnurre/external-GIT/fmd-android CypherUtils.java\n(an FOSS client) and FmdServerApiV1Repository.kt. Server-side\nhashing was verified by reading /Users/tschnurre/external-GIT/fmd-server\nuser/password.go.\n\nLibrary choice: hash-wasm (not argon2). The npm argon2 package\nenforces timeCost >= 2, but the FMD spec requires timeCost = 1.\nhash-wasm accepts t=1 and produces the same PHC output as the\nAndroid Bouncy Castle implementation. Performance is irrelevant\nfor a once-per-login operation (98 ms vs 25 ms).\n\nVerified against the live server with the smoke script:\n  scripts/auth-smoke.mjs (new) runs FmdAuth.authenticate() against\n  a real FMD server using env-var credentials and prints the\n  result. Exit 0 on success, 1 on auth failure, 2 on missing env.\n\nSmoke test output (sanitized):\n  FMD authentication successful\n  OK access_token=PCDPaFVd... private_key=YAs2eZEX...\n\nBug D (the last blocker from the add-admin-ui-index-html\nchange''s out-of-scope follow-ups) is now resolved.","tree":{"sha":"fe5d6c192fb3ad605515ef36ce1f5f96efece984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/trees/fe5d6c192fb3ad605515ef36ce1f5f96efece984"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/commits/ff37212a8e2155dbb5d31a5025a19a724c57dc27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/ff37212a8e2155dbb5d31a5025a19a724c57dc27","node_id":"C_kwDOSw1L3toAKGZmMzcyMTJhOGUyMTU1ZGJiNWQzMWE1MDI1YTE5YTcyNGM1N2RjMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3","sha":"0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3"}],"sha":"ff37212a8e2155dbb5d31a5025a19a724c57dc27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/ff37212a8e2155dbb5d31a5025a19a724c57dc27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T14:34:52Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T14:34:52Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"message":"scripts: add auth-smoke-stub probe for FMD server salt endpoint\n\nThrowaway script that hits POST /salt against a real FMD server and\nprints the raw response. Used in OpenSpec change fix-auth-bug Task\n1.1 to identify that the field name is IDT, not id or username, and\nthat the salt comes back as URL-safe Base64 with no padding.\n\nNot part of the adapter runtime; lives in scripts/ for ad-hoc\ndebugging.","tree":{"sha":"342a29feb647edb7ac59c8049d7f192659f57a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/trees/342a29feb647edb7ac59c8049d7f192659f57a84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/commits/0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3","node_id":"C_kwDOSw1L3toAKDAwMjlmNDQwZmQ4MzE0YzYwNzNjNTgzYTY1ZTM1ZjJjZGI4N2IwYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599","sha":"5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599"}],"sha":"0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/0029f440fd8314c6073c583a65e35f2cdb87b0a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T14:34:48Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T14:34:48Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"message":"docs(change): expand fix-auth-bug scope from 2 to 5 coupled bugs\n\nThe original proposal assumed two bugs (PBKDF2 instead of Argon2id,\nURL-safe Base64 not handled). The spike against the FMD server source\nat /Users/tschnurre/external-GIT/fmd-server tag v0.14.0 (matching the\nrunning container) revealed three more:\n\n  3. The endpoint paths are wrong. The current code targets\n     GET /api/v1/auth/salt and POST /api/v1/auth/login. The real\n     server uses POST /salt (with {IDT} in the body), POST\n     /requestAccess (with {IDT, PasswordHash, SessionDurationSeconds}),\n     and POST /key. The old paths return the webui HTML, not JSON.\n\n  4. The two-step KDF architecture is missing. The client must run\n     Argon2id once to produce a PHC-encoded string, then send only\n     the hash portion of that string as PasswordHash to\n     /requestAccess. The current deriveKey is missing this entirely\n     and sends the raw plaintext-derived value.\n\n  5. getPrivateKey is GET with IDT header. The real endpoint is POST\n     /key with {IDT: <accessToken>} in the body, returning the PEM\n     in the Data field.\n\nThis commit updates proposal.md, design.md, and the fmd-auth spec\nto reflect all five bugs. The fmd-auth-testing spec was already\ngeneric enough to cover the new flow and is unchanged.\n\nSpike findings (Tasks 1.1-1.3) are also captured in tasks.md so the\nnext implementer does not have to re-derive them. The new script\nscripts/auth-smoke-stub.mjs is committed alongside as the spike\nartefact.","tree":{"sha":"7caaa5f0cb13fa826db01f56ecd769e44ccc685a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/trees/7caaa5f0cb13fa826db01f56ecd769e44ccc685a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/commits/5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599","node_id":"C_kwDOSw1L3toAKDViMDg1NmM3OGU2YTM4YTU0OTMwMDc0ZDg3NjlmMmJkZWEzNzM1OTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df","sha":"10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df"}],"sha":"5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/5b0856c78e6a38a54930074d8769f2bdea373599"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:47:05Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:47:05Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"message":"build: rebuild for ff2286d\n\nThe previous commit (fix(adapter)) was on src/main.ts; tsc --build\nemitted the matching build/main.js. The Docker container reads\nbuild/main.js, not the .ts source, so this commit is the\ncompanion build output.","tree":{"sha":"b04d5ae61d3295e8a09ecb942c3ce1376b36558c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/trees/b04d5ae61d3295e8a09ecb942c3ce1376b36558c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/commits/10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df","node_id":"C_kwDOSw1L3toAKDEwODk0ZGUxOTIzMDMzMmJkMjlhNjZmN2QzZWE4YjUzZmE2MTkxZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba","sha":"ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba"}],"sha":"10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/10894de19230332bd29a66f7d3ea8b53fa6191df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:46:49Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:46:49Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"message":"fix(adapter): wire FMD auth, device fetch, and ring-state subscribe\n\nOUT OF SCOPE for the OpenSpec change add-admin-ui-index-html, but\ndiscovered while testing the new Admin-UI: the adapter never made\nan API call to the FMD server, never loaded devices, and never\nsubscribed to the userdata ring states. Symptom: setting\n0_userdata.0.FindMyDevice.ring.eLZo3 = true does nothing.\n\nThree coupled bugs in src/main.ts:\n\n  A. onReady created FmdAuth but never called authenticate(), so\n     no tokens were exchanged and no FmdApi instance was ever\n     built. fetchDevices() therefore never ran, which is why no\n     device states under 0_userdata.0.FindMyDevice.ring.<id> were\n     ever created as State objects. The setState from the GUI\n     ended up writing a value to a non-existent state slot.\n\n  B. onReady subscribed to the hardcoded Shelly button only.\n     subscribeStates(''0_userdata.0.FindMyDevice.ring.*'') was\n     missing entirely, so onStateChange never fired for userdata\n     ring changes. The regex in onStateChange was correct but\n     unreachable.\n\n  C. The hardcoded BUTTON_STATE_ID was used in both subscribe and\n     in the onStateChange comparison, ignoring the buttonStateId\n     field we just added to the native schema. Now the configured\n     value takes precedence; the hardcoded value is the fallback\n     for users who do not configure the new field.\n\nFix:\n\n  - onReady kicks off a background connectAndFetchDevices() that\n    runs fmdAuth.authenticate(), builds FmdApi with the resulting\n    tokens, calls fetchDevices(), and sets connectionStatus.\n  - onReady additionally subscribes to the userdata ring pattern.\n  - subscribeToButtonState and onStateChange resolve the button\n    id from config.buttonStateId first, falling back to the\n    hardcoded value.\n\nAfter this change, the adapter log will show ''connecting'' and\n''connected'' lines after ''FMD adapter ready'', and setting\n0_userdata.0.FindMyDevice.ring.eLZo3 = true should produce\n''Ring state triggered for device: eLZo3'' in the log and call\nFmdApi.sendRingCommand.","tree":{"sha":"0257597283b30b7206246029d243b4f8a92af637","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/trees/0257597283b30b7206246029d243b4f8a92af637"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/commits/ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba","node_id":"C_kwDOSw1L3toAKGZmMjI4NmQwMTYxMDNlZTY2ZjAxZGQyOTMzYTk3ZmEzMDg3MmE0YmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03","sha":"cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03"}],"sha":"ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/ff2286d016103ee66f01dd2933a97fa30872a4ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:30:09Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:30:09Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"message":"fix(admin): strip unknown jsonConfig fields to pass meta-schema validation\n\nThe controller''s jsonConfig meta-schema rejected the previous schema\nwith three errors: validator must be a string (we had an object),\nthe connection panel''s allOf/if/then didn''t match, and the\ntop-level if/else didn''t match.\n\nTo unblock the wrench pop-up immediately we strip the unsupported\nfields:\n  - serverUrl.validator (object form)\n  - ringDeviceId/buttonStateId.validator: null\n  - the testConnection sendTo button (and its result sub-object)\n  - placeholder fields (kept for now; not validated but unused)\n\nWhat stays:\n  - all four text/password items (connection + hardware trigger)\n  - the staticText items for status and devices panels\n  - the JsonConfig-native panel/item layout\n\nA follow-up change will re-add the Test Connection sendTo button\nonce the jsonConfig meta-schema for the result sub-object is\nconfirmed. The user can trigger rings today via the\n0_userdata.0.FindMyDevice.ring.<deviceId> state, which is the\ndocumented path.","tree":{"sha":"89a93f339e941d5bc06a09d6db73e3cf4731ce97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/trees/89a93f339e941d5bc06a09d6db73e3cf4731ce97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/commits/cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03","node_id":"C_kwDOSw1L3toAKGNkMjVmZTAzMGUzNTJjYzgxNzdmZTk0OWQ3MThjNjkyZGVlMDBkMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commit/14bd5d69fc38938685044db05b32008a5e9ab171","sha":"14bd5d69fc38938685044db05b32008a5e9ab171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/14bd5d69fc38938685044db05b32008a5e9ab171"}],"sha":"cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/cd25fe030e352cc8177fe949d718c692dee00d03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/toBYTEas","id":225377338,"login":"toBYTEas","node_id":"U_kgDODW78Og","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/commits/14bd5d69fc38938685044db05b32008a5e9ab171/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:18:32Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-08T13:18:32Z","email":"tschnurre@ethz.ch","name":"tschnurre"},"message":"feat(admin): ship Vite-built admin UI to fix wrench pop-up 404\n\nioBroker.admin 7.7.22 always loads the wrench pop-up as an iframe\npointing at admin/index.html (or admin/index_m.html for materialize).\nWithout an index.html, the browser logs a 404 and the config form\nfails to load. The adminUI.config = ''json'' flag does not skip the\niframe — it only governs the Instances list and the sidebar tab.\n\nThis change adds:\n\n  - src-admin/ source tree (React 18 + Vite + @iobroker/json-config)\n  - admin/index.html, admin/index_m.html, admin/assets/ build output\n    (committed so the Docker dev container needs no Node toolchain)\n  - admin/jsonConfig.json5 form definition (source-of-truth in\n    src-admin/schema.json5, copied on build)\n  - io-package.json: ringDeviceId and buttonStateId in the native\n    schema so the hardware button trigger is configurable from the UI\n  - io-package.json: adminUI.config = ''json'', no adminUI.tab (setting\n    tab forces the loader to probe for tab.html/tab_m.html and break\n    the pop-up with a ''Cannot find tab(_m).html'' alert)\n  - src-admin/socket.ts: small adapter-socket wrapper that reuses the\n    host admin''s window.io global and exposes the getStates/getState/\n    setObject/sendTo/subscribeState surface JsonConfig expects\n  - scripts/build-admin.mjs: build wrapper that wipes only Vite\n    outputs from admin/, leaves settings.json and favicon.ico alone\n  - CLAUDE.md: deployment workflow now has 9 steps including the\n    npm run build:admin pre-step and the iobroker-data/files/<adapter>/\n    io-package.json touch for adminUI flag changes\n  - docs/admin-ui.md, README.md updates, investigation cross-link\n\nOut of scope (separate changes): singleInstance: true enforcement,\nthe package.json name drift (iobroker.fmd vs iobroker-fmd), and the\niobroker upload not refreshing iobroker-data/files/<adapter>/io-package.json\non its own.","tree":{"sha":"bc1caa68187aa8f2045487c9ccde1e9e109b653c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/trees/bc1caa68187aa8f2045487c9ccde1e9e109b653c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/realrubbish/iobroker-fmd/git/commits/14bd5d69fc38938685044db05b32008a5e9ab171","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/225377338?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/toBYTEas/events{