:{"date":"2026-07-23T18:07:23Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T18:07:23Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"fix(ui): consistent trigger row alignment in jCustomer → SFDC\n\nThe outbound Triggers switches were laid out switch-left/text-right via inline\nflex, inconsistent with the inbound (SFDC → jCustomer) triggers (text-left,\ncontrol-right). Aligned all rows — target object, profile-update, form-submission,\nand schedule-enable — to the shared .triggerRow/.triggerInfo pattern (label left,\ncontrol right-aligned), matching the inbound tab. Added those classes to the CSS\nmodule the tab imports.","tree":{"sha":"226405f185ad16e354419662c92ec20cc027cf98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/trees/226405f185ad16e354419662c92ec20cc027cf98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/commits/05bff2624b6499ada41423b70c00f23d8b3b7fbd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/05bff2624b6499ada41423b70c00f23d8b3b7fbd","node_id":"C_kwDOSw3eDtoAKDA1YmZmMjYyNGI2NDk5YWRhNDE0MjNiNzBjMDBmMjNkOGIzYjdmYmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b","sha":"37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b"}],"sha":"05bff2624b6499ada41423b70c00f23d8b3b7fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/05bff2624b6499ada41423b70c00f23d8b3b7fbd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T18:02:51Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T18:02:51Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"feat: sub-hourly cron builder — \"Every N minutes\" frequency\n\nAdds a \"Minutes\" frequency to the shared CronBuilder so schedules down to every\nminute are configurable in the friendly UI (not just hourly+). Additive — the\nexisting Hour/Day/Week/Month options are unchanged, and it''s available to both the\ninbound and outbound schedules.\n\n- buildCron: minutes → \"0 0/N * * * ?\"; parseCron detects a \"0/N\" (or \"*/N\") minute\n  step → freq=minutes, interval=N (round-trips).\n- Interval options: 1, 5, 10, 15, 20, 30.\n- en/fr locales: cron.freq.minutes + cron.minutesUnit.\n\nVerified live: outbound schedule set to every 5 minutes (\"0 0/5 * * * ?\") — the\nQuartz reconcile job accepted and registered it.","tree":{"sha":"9b0d71991d267b86be3e494425dc3e5352b791cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/trees/9b0d71991d267b86be3e494425dc3e5352b791cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/commits/37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b","node_id":"C_kwDOSw3eDtoAKDM3ZDM4MTRjNjFlMDE0YmIxMzI2MzY3Y2E5N2E0MWNlZjI4OWU3N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374","sha":"ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374"}],"sha":"37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/37d3814c61e014bb1326367ca97a41cef289e77b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:48:10Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:48:10Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"fix+ux: outbound reconcile scheduler + friendly cron builder\n\nFix (why console edits weren''t auto-syncing): SfdcOutboundReconcileJob.applySchedule\nunscheduled the trigger but re-added the job via scheduleJob(jobDetail, trigger),\nwhich throws ObjectAlreadyExistsException once the job is already stored (e.g. from\na previous enable) — swallowed by the save, so re-enabling silently did nothing.\nNow deletes the job before scheduling (mirrors SfdcSyncJob). Verified live: the\nQuartz poll fires on schedule and save→reschedule logs cleanly.\n\nUX: the jCustomer → SFDC schedule now uses the same CronBuilder as SFDC → jCustomer\n(Every Hour/Day/Week/Month + time/day dropdowns) instead of a raw cron field.\nDefault cron is hourly (\"0 0 * * * ?\", the builder''s finest granularity); use\n\"Sync now\" for an immediate run.","tree":{"sha":"52298ef36fce44cc01179904811980b3e9e2376d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/trees/52298ef36fce44cc01179904811980b3e9e2376d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/commits/ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374","node_id":"C_kwDOSw3eDtoAKGFlMjczOGYzOTdhMjA0OGE0N2MyZmY1OTA4NmM2MmY2NzAyMjkzNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2","sha":"2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2"}],"sha":"ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/ae2738f397a2048a47c2ff59086c62f670229374"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:32:13Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:32:13Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"feat: outbound targets a single object (Lead OR Contact), not both\n\nPer feedback: pushing a profile to both Lead and Contact when both were mapped was\nundesirable. Add an outboundObject setting (Lead | Contact) so the sync targets\nexactly one.\n\n- ConnectorConfigService: outboundObject in outbound triggers (default Lead).\n- SfdcOutboundSyncService.pushProfile: push only to the configured target object\n  (no longer iterates both); warns if that object has no mapping.\n- SaveOutboundTriggersAction: persist outboundObject.\n- UI: \"Target Salesforce object\" dropdown (Lead / Contact) in the jCustomer → SFDC\n  Triggers tab; en/fr locales. Field mapping for both objects still lives in the\n  Mapping tab; only the selected target is synced.\n\nVerified live: target=Lead pushed only the Lead; target=Contact attempted only the\nContact (neither touched the other object).","tree":{"sha":"0d8d48e258b23d604dc4e6c1a2a313a9d6e56552","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/trees/0d8d48e258b23d604dc4e6c1a2a313a9d6e56552"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/commits/2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2","node_id":"C_kwDOSw3eDtoAKDJlZmU1YjAxMTEwMTEzYjgzNDNiZDNjMTQ0OWM1YWY4MGI3ZDE3YTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7","sha":"8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7"}],"sha":"2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/2efe5b01110113b8343bd3c1449c5af80b7d17a2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:24:14Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:24:14Z","email":"smonier@jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"message":"chore: start 2.1.0-SNAPSHOT development","tree":{"sha":"c284d1c7a9484eb49a629f55cb7a52345d39b48e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/trees/c284d1c7a9484eb49a629f55cb7a52345d39b48e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/commits/8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7","node_id":"C_kwDOSw3eDtoAKDhjZjBiOWNlODM1MTRjZTk4OTE4NGEzY2Y3ZWI5ZjZmNmNlZTNjZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commit/521ddd21b0b6c5e92ff0921c2f243450af592586","sha":"521ddd21b0b6c5e92ff0921c2f243450af592586","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/521ddd21b0b6c5e92ff0921c2f243450af592586"}],"sha":"8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/8cf0b9ce83514ce989184a3cf7eb9f6f6cee3ce7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/722535?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smonier","id":722535,"login":"smonier","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMjUzNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smonier","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/commits/521ddd21b0b6c5e92ff0921c2f243450af592586/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:19:24Z","email":"smonier@Jahia.com","name":"Stephane Monier"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T17:19:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bidirectional jCustomer ⇄ Salesforce sync (v2.0.0) (#2)\n\n* feat: add Salesforce Lead object to mapping UI and sync\n\nAdds Lead alongside Contact and Account.\n\n- UI (MappingTab): Lead tab; object handling generalized (state derived from\n  SFDC_OBJECTS) so fields/mappings are no longer hardcoded per object.\n- GetSfdcFieldsAction: describe Lead too, each object guarded independently so\n  one object''s failure (e.g. no Lead access) no longer blanks the others.\n- GetMappingAction: returns Lead mappings (iterates SFDC_OBJECTS).\n- SfdcSyncService: Lead is a top-level object matched to jCustomer profiles by\n  email (no Account relationship, no stored ContactId). buildLeadSoql +\n  processLead; wired into both batch sync and login sync. Converted leads are\n  excluded (IsConverted = false) since they already exist as Contacts.\n- Locales (en/fr) and README updated to mention Lead.\n\nConnectorConfigService needed no change — load/saveMapping are object-generic.\n\nVerified live: getSfdcFields returns Lead (73 fields from Salesforce),\ngetMapping exposes the Lead key.\n\n* feat: jCustomer → SFDC outbound sync (Lead) — Phases 2–3\n\nAdds the jCustomer → Salesforce direction (targets Lead) alongside the existing\nSFDC → jCustomer sync, with the connection shared by both directions.\n\nUI (Phase 2 restructure):\n- SfdcAdmin reorganized into: Connection (shared) | SFDC → jCustomer (inbound) |\n  jCustomer → SFDC (outbound). InboundPanel groups the existing Mapping+Sync tabs.\n- OutboundPanel + OutboundMappingTab (jC property → Lead field; flags that\n  LastName+Company are required to create Leads) + OutboundSyncTab (targeted\n  \"Push now\" by email + last-run state). api.js + en/fr locales.\n\nWrite path (Phase 3):\n- SfdcApiClient: createSObject/updateSObject (POST/PATCH, 401-retry) +\n  findLeadIdByEmail; shared dataBaseUrl helper.\n- SfdcOutboundSyncService: map jC props → Lead fields, resolve by stored\n  SFDC_LeadId then email, update-or-create (create guarded on LastName+Company),\n  write SFDC_LeadId back to the profile for idempotency.\n- ConnectorConfigService: outbound mapping (refactored shared load/save helpers)\n  + outbound sync state under /outbound.\n- Actions (extend AbstractSfdcAdminAction, added to CSRF whitelist):\n  getOutboundMapping / saveOutboundMapping / triggerOutboundSync /\n  getOutboundSyncState.\n\nVerified live (no real Salesforce writes): mapping persists + reads back, a push\nfor a non-existent profile is a safe no-op, security gate (cross-origin 403) applies.\n\nDeferred: Phase 4 outbound trigger config UI, Phase 5 event webhook (needs a custom\nUnomi ActionExecutor + rule — spike confirmed no stock webhook action exists),\nPhase 6 scheduled reconcile.\n\n* feat: outbound event-trigger config (profile update + form submission) — Phase 4\n\nAdds the outbound trigger configuration for the two jCustomer events that will\ndrive the jCustomer → SFDC push:\n- On profile update (profile must have an email to match/create the Lead)\n- On form submission\nplus a master enable switch (off by default until the event webhook is deployed).\n\n- ConnectorConfigService: load/saveOutboundTriggers under /outbound/triggers\n  (enabled, onProfileUpdate, onFormSubmission).\n- Actions: getOutboundTriggers / saveOutboundTriggers (extend AbstractSfdcAdminAction,\n  added to CSRF whitelist).\n- UI: OutboundTriggersTab (Switch toggles) added as an outbound sub-tab; api.js +\n  en/fr locales (incl. the \"email required\" note on profile-update).\n\nVerified live: defaults load, save persists, security gate applies. These toggles\nparameterize the Unomi rule that Phase 5 (event webhook) will deploy.\n\n* feat: outbound event webhook endpoint (Jahia side) — Phase 5a\n\nSecured server-to-server endpoint that jCustomer (Unomi) calls when a monitored\nevent fires, to push the profile to Salesforce as a Lead.\n\n- SfdcOutboundWebhookAction: a public Action (requireAuthenticatedUser=false, no\n  admin/same-origin gate — Unomi is not a browser) dispatched on a guest-readable\n  live node (/cms/render/live/en/sites/systemsite.sfdcOutboundWebhook.do).\n  Authenticated by a shared secret (X-Sfdc-Webhook-Secret, constant-time compare);\n  fail-closed (503) if unset. Only capability: push the given email through the\n  configured Lead mapping. The SF push runs on a background thread so the response\n  returns immediately (Unomi runs rule actions synchronously).\n- ConnectorConfigService.getOrCreateWebhookSecret(): secret stored in JCR (survives\n  redeploys, never committed) rather than the OSGi config (which the module re-applies\n  on deploy). Auto-generated (SecureRandom) on first use.\n- CSRF whitelist += sfdcOutboundWebhook.\n\nVerified live: no secret → 403; correct secret + bogus email → accepted (async\nno-op). Note: a root-path OSGi whiteboard servlet was tried first but Jahia''s\nrender/urlrewrite shadows root paths, so the Action transport is used instead.\n\n* feat: event-driven outbound trigger — Unomi action bundle + rules (Phase 5b)\n\nCompletes the hybrid outbound trigger: real jCustomer events now push profiles to\nSalesforce as Leads via the Jahia webhook.\n\nNew sub-project unomi-sfdc-webhook/ (a separate OSGi bundle deployed into the\njCustomer/Unomi Karaf container, NOT into Jahia — Unomi ships no stock HTTP action):\n- SfdcWebhookActionExecutor: custom Unomi ActionExecutor (id sfdcWebhook) that\n  fire-and-forget POSTs {email,eventType} to the Jahia webhook with the shared\n  secret header. Non-blocking (Unomi runs actions synchronously in the pipeline);\n  no-op unless the profile has an email.\n- META-INF/cxs/actions/sfdcWebhookAction.json: action-type registration.\n- rules/: the two rules (form submission; profile update when email present),\n  with JAHIA_HOST + secret placeholders. Loop-safe: profile-update keys on\n  updateProperties, distinct from the inbound updateUserEfficyPortalData event.\n- README with build + deploy recipe.\n\nVerified LIVE end-to-end: a form event for a real mysoprahr profile flowed\nUnomi rule → sfdcWebhookAction → secured Jahia webhook → outbound Lead push\n(\"Accepted push for email=…\"). Secret lives in JCR (survives redeploys).\n\nReconcile job (Phase 6) still to come to complete the \"hybrid\" (webhook + poll).\n\n* fix: outbound trigger switches stuck off — read e.target.checked (moonstone Switch onChange gives the event, not a checked arg)\n\n* feat: outbound reconcile (scheduled + manual) — Phase 6\n\nCompletes the hybrid outbound trigger. The event webhook only fires on Unomi\nevents (tracker/form/eventcollector); direct profile edits (console/REST/batch)\nemit no event, so they never reached Salesforce. The reconcile sweep closes that\ngap by pushing profiles changed since the last run.\n\n- JCustomerProfileService.searchProfilesModifiedSince: query profiles with\n  systemProperties.lastUpdated >= cutoff AND an email (newest first).\n- SfdcOutboundSyncService.runReconcile: push each changed profile (idempotent via\n  the stored SFDC_LeadId); advance the watermark; record state. First run looks\n  back 24h.\n- SfdcOutboundReconcileJob: Quartz job driven by the JCR reconcile config\n  (reconcileEnabled / reconcileCron); reschedules when the triggers config is saved.\n- TriggerOutboundReconcileAction: manual \"Reconcile now\".\n- Config: reconcile settings in outbound triggers + lastReconcileAt.\n- UI: reconcile section (enable + cron + Reconcile now) in the Triggers tab;\n  api.js + en/fr locales.\n- CSRF whitelist += triggerOutboundReconcile.\n\nVerified live: \"Reconcile now\" swept 7 changed profiles and updated 6 Leads —\nincluding pam (Lead Title = jobTitle), resolving the reported case. Enabling the\nschedule reschedules the Quartz job (every 15 min by default). SF constraints\nhandled gracefully: create needs LastName+Company (else skipped with a warning);\nSF duplicate rule → logged error, run continues.\n\n* refactor: poll-only outbound sync (align with Jahia Workato Unomi connector); retire event webhook\n\nReviewed Jahia/workato-unomi-connector: its new_or_updated_profile and new_event\ntriggers are POLL-based (/cxs/profiles/search on systemProperties.lastUpdated,\n/cxs/events/search on timeStamp) — no custom Unomi action, no webhook. Adopting\nthat simpler, canonical approach and retiring the Phase 5 event machinery.\n\nPoll (SfdcOutboundSyncService.runReconcile now polls two ways, gated by toggles):\n- Profiles changed since the watermark (greaterThan, sorted by lastUpdated),\n  excluding the healthCheck profile and non-UUID itemIds (per the Workato connector).\n- Form events since the watermark (/cxs/events/search, eventType=form) → push each\n  event''s profile once (deduped against the profile poll).\n- JCustomerProfileService: searchFormEventsSince + getProfileById added; profile\n  search refined (greaterThan + healthCheck exclusion).\n\nRetired (event webhook, Phase 5):\n- Removed SfdcOutboundWebhookAction + its CSRF entry + the JCR webhook secret.\n- Deleted the unomi-sfdc-webhook OSGi bundle sub-project; undeployed it from the\n  jcustomer container and deleted the two Unomi rules.\n\nUI: Triggers tab reframed to poll-only — \"What to sync\" (profile updates / form\nsubmissions toggles, gating both scheduled and manual runs) + \"Schedule\"\n(enable + cron + \"Sync now\"). en/fr locales updated.\n\nVerified live: \"Sync now\" polled profiles + form events, updated a Lead, 0 errors;\nwebhook action no longer registered.\n\n* feat: add Contact as an outbound (jCustomer → SFDC) target alongside Lead\n\nOutbound sync now pushes to Lead and/or Contact — whichever has a mapping.\n\n- SfdcOutboundSyncService: pushProfile iterates OUTBOUND_OBJECTS {Lead, Contact};\n  per-object mapping, id property (SFDC_LeadId / SFDC_ContactId — the latter also\n  set by the inbound Contact sync, so round-trips update the same Contact), email\n  match, and per-object create requirements (Lead: LastName+Company; Contact:\n  LastName). Record id written back to the profile for idempotency.\n- SfdcApiClient.findLeadIdByEmail → findSObjectIdByEmail(type, email) (Contact has\n  no IsConverted filter).\n- GetOutboundMappingAction returns Lead + Contact.\n- OutboundMappingTab: Lead/Contact object tabs; per-object required-field hint.\n- en/fr locales: per-object ({{obj}}) mapping messages.\n\nVerified live: one push of pam@luxe.com updated the linked Lead AND created a\nContact (003TE…), 4 fields each; SFDC_ContactId stored back on the profile.\n\n* docs+release: bidirectional README; version 2.0.0","tree":{"sha":"f7c84ac6da02d92239bc0e6f6b8c39dbc172e416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/trees/f7c84ac6da02d92239bc0e6f6b8c39dbc172e416"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/jcustomer-sfdc-connector/git/commits/521ddd21b0b6c5e92ff0921c2f243450af592586","verification":{"payload":"tree f7c84ac6da02d92239bc0e6f6b8c39dbc172e416\nparent 09cf87efb96f2d4f454232bde53dd74edefcbf46\nauthor Stephane Monier <smonier@Jahia.com> 1784827164 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784827164 +0200\n\nBidirectional jCustomer ⇄ Salesforce sync (v2.0.0) (#2)\n\n* feat: add Salesforce Lead object to mapping UI and sync\n\nAdds Lead alongside Contact and Account.\n\n- UI (MappingTab): Lead tab; object handling generalized (state derived from\n  SFDC_OBJECTS) so fields/mappings are no longer hardcoded per object.\n- GetSfdcFieldsAction: describe Lead too, each object guarded independently so\n  one object''s failure (e.g. no Lead access) no longer blanks the others.\n- GetMappingAction: returns Lead mappings (iterates SFDC_OBJECTS).\n- SfdcSyncService: Lead is a top-level object matched to jCustomer profiles by\n  email (no Account relationship, no stored ContactId). buildLeadSoql +\n  processLead; wired into both batch sync and login sync. Converted leads are\n  excluded (IsConverted = false) since they already exist as Contacts.\n- Locales (en/fr) and README updated to mention Lead.\n\nConnectorConfigService needed no change — load/saveMapping are object-generic.\n\nVerified live: getSfdcFields returns Lead (73 fields from Salesforce),\ngetMapping exposes the Lead key.\n\n* feat: jCustomer → SFDC outbound sync (Lead) — Phases 2–3\n\nAdds the jCustomer → Salesforce direction (targets Lead) alongside the existing\nSFDC → jCustomer sync, with the connection shared by both directions.\n\nUI (Phase 2 restructure):\n- SfdcAdmin reorganized into: Connection (shared) | SFDC → jCustomer (inbound) |\n  jCustomer → SFDC (outbound). InboundPanel groups the existing Mapping+Sync tabs.\n- OutboundPanel + OutboundMappingTab (jC property → Lead field; flags that\n  LastName+Company are required to create Leads) + OutboundSyncTab (targeted\n  \"Push now\" by email + last-run state). api.js + en/fr locales.\n\nWrite path (Phase 3):\n- SfdcApiClient: createSObject/updateSObject (POST/PATCH, 401-retry) +\n  findLeadIdByEmail; shared dataBaseUrl helper.\n- SfdcOutboundSyncService: map jC props → Lead fields, resolve by stored\n  SFDC_LeadId then email, update-or-create (create guarded on LastName+Company),\n  write SFDC_LeadId back to the profile for idempotency.\n- ConnectorConfigService: outbound mapping (refactored shared load/save helpers)\n  + outbound sync state under /outbound.\n- Actions (extend AbstractSfdcAdminAction, added to CSRF whitelist):\n  getOutboundMapping / saveOutboundMapping / triggerOutboundSync /\n  getOutboundSyncState.\n\nVerified live (no real Salesforce writes): mapping persists + reads back, a push\nfor a non-existent profile is a safe no-op, security gate (cross-origin 403) applies.\n\nDeferred: Phase 4 outbound trigger config UI, Phase 5 event webhook (needs a custom\nUnomi ActionExecutor + rule — spike confirmed no stock webhook action exists),\nPhase 6 scheduled reconcile.\n\n* feat: outbound event-trigger config (profile update + form submission) — Phase 4\n\nAdds the outbound trigger configuration for the two jCustomer events that will\ndrive the jCustomer → SFDC push:\n- On profile update (profile must have an email to match/create the Lead)\n- On form submission\nplus a master enable switch (off by default until the event webhook is deployed).\n\n- ConnectorConfigService: load/saveOutboundTriggers under /outbound/triggers\n  (enabled, onProfileUpdate, onFormSubmission).\n- Actions: getOutboundTriggers / saveOutboundTriggers (extend AbstractSfdcAdminAction,\n  added to CSRF whitelist).\n- UI: OutboundTriggersTab (Switch toggles) added as an outbound sub-tab; api.js +\n  en/fr locales (incl. the \"email required\" note on profile-update).\n\nVerified live: defaults load, save persists, security gate applies. These toggles\nparameterize the Unomi rule that Phase 5 (event webhook) will deploy.\n\n* feat: outbound event webhook endpoint (Jahia side) — Phase 5a\n\nSecured server-to-server endpoint that jCustomer (Unomi) calls when a monitored\nevent fires, to push the profile to Salesforce as a Lead.\n\n- SfdcOutboundWebhookAction: a public Action (requireAuthenticatedUser=false, no\n  admin/same-origin gate — Unomi is not a browser) dispatched on a guest-readable\n  live node (/cms/render/live/en/sites/systemsite.sfdcOutboundWebhook.do).\n  Authenticated by a shared secret (X-Sfdc-Webhook-Secret, constant-time compare);\n  fail-closed (503) if unset. Only capability: push the given email through the\n  configured Lead mapping. The SF push runs on a background thread so the response\n  returns immediately (Unomi runs rule actions synchronously).\n- ConnectorConfigService.getOrCreateWebhookSecret(): secret stored in JCR (survives\n  redeploys, never committed) rather than the OSGi config (which the module re-applies\n  on deploy). Auto-generated (SecureRandom) on first use.\n- CSRF whitelist += sfdcOutboundWebhook.\n\nVerified live: no secret → 403; correct secret + bogus email → accepted (async\nno-op). Note: a root-path OSGi whiteboard servlet was tried first but Jahia''s\nrender/urlrewrite shadows root paths, so the Action transport is used instead.\n\n* feat: event-driven outbound trigger — Unomi action bundle + rules (Phase 5b)\n\nCompletes the hybrid outbound trigger: real jCustomer events now push profiles to\nSalesforce as Leads via the Jahia webhook.\n\nNew sub-project unomi-sfdc-webhook/ (a separate OSGi bundle deployed into the\njCustomer/Unomi Karaf container, NOT into Jahia — Unomi ships no stock HTTP action):\n- SfdcWebhookActionExecutor: custom Unomi ActionExecutor (id sfdcWebhook) that\n  fire-and-forget POSTs {email,eventType} to the Jahia webhook with the shared\n  secret header. Non-blocking (Unomi runs actions synchronously in the pipeline);\n  no-op unless the profile has an email.\n- META-INF/cxs/actions/sfdcWebhookAction.json: action-type registration.\n- rules/: the two rules (form submission; profile update when email present),\n  with JAHIA_HOST + secret placeholders. Loop-safe: profile-update keys on\n  updateProperties, distinct from the inbound updateUserEfficyPortalData event.\n- README with build + deploy recipe.\n\nVerified LIVE end-to-end: a form event for a real mysoprahr profile flowed\nUnomi rule → sfdcWebhookAction → secured Jahia webhook → outbound Lead push\n(\"Accepted push for email=…\"). Secret lives in JCR (survives redeploys).\n\nReconcile job (Phase 6) still to come to complete the \"hybrid\" (webhook + poll).\n\n* fix: outbound trigger switches stuck off — read e.target.checked (moonstone Switch onChange gives the event, not a checked arg)\n\n* feat: outbound reconcile (scheduled + manual) — Phase 6\n\nCompletes the hybrid outbound trigger. The event webhook only fires on Unomi\nevents (tracker/form/eventcollector); direct profile edits (console/REST/batch)\nemit no event, so they never reached Salesforce. The reconcile sweep closes that\ngap by pushing profiles changed since the last run.\n\n- JCustomerProfileService.searchProfilesModifiedSince: query profiles with\n  systemProperties.lastUpdated >= cutoff AND an email (newest first).\n- SfdcOutboundSyncService.runReconcile: push each changed profile (idempotent via\n  the stored SFDC_LeadId); advance the watermark; record state. First run looks\n  back 24h.\n- SfdcOutboundReconcileJob: Quartz job driven by the JCR reconcile config\n  (reconcileEnabled / reconcileCron); reschedules when the triggers config is saved.\n- TriggerOutboundReconcileAction: manual \"Reconcile now\".\n- Config: reconcile settings in outbound triggers + lastReconcileAt.\n- UI: reconcile section (enable + cron + Reconcile now) in the Triggers tab;\n  api.js + en/fr locales.\n- CSRF whitelist += triggerOutboundReconcile.\n\nVerified live: \"Reconcile now\" swept 7 changed profiles and updated 6 Leads —\nincluding pam (Lead Title = jobTitle), resolving the reported case. Enabling the\nschedule reschedules the Quartz job (every 15 min by default). SF constraints\nhandled gracefully: create needs LastName+Company (else skipped with a warning);\nSF duplicate rule → logged error, run continues.\n\n* refactor: poll-only outbound sync (align with Jahia Workato Unomi connector); retire event webhook\n\nReviewed Jahia/workato-unomi-connector: its new_or_updated_profile and new_event\ntriggers are POLL-based (/cxs/profiles/search on systemProperties.lastUpdated,\n/cxs/events/search on timeStamp) — no custom Unomi action, no webhook. Adopting\nthat simpler, canonical approach and retiring the Phase 5 event machinery.\n\nPoll (SfdcOutboundSyncService.runReconcile now polls two ways, gated by toggles):\n- Profiles changed since the watermark (greaterThan, sorted by lastUpdated),\n  excluding the healthCheck profile and non-UUID itemIds (per the Workato connector).\n- Form events since the watermark (/cxs/events/search, eventType=form) → push each\n  event''s profile once (deduped against the profile poll).\n- JCustomerProfileService: searchFormEventsSince + getProfileById added; profile\n  search refined (greaterThan + healthCheck exclusion).\n\nRetired (event webhook, Phase 5):\n- Removed SfdcOutboundWebhookAction + its CSRF entry + the JCR webhook secret.\n- Deleted the unomi-sfdc-webhook OSGi bundle sub-project; undeployed it from the\n  jcustomer container and deleted the two Unomi rules.\n\nUI: Triggers tab reframed to poll-only — \"What to sync\" (profile updates / form\nsubmissions toggles, gating both scheduled and manual runs) + \"Schedule\"\n(enable + cron + \"Sync now\"). en/fr locales updated.\n\nVerified live: \"Sync now\" polled profiles + form events, updated a Lead, 0 errors;\nwebhook action no longer registered.\n\n* feat: add Contact as an outbound (jCustomer → SFDC) target alongside Lead\n\nOutbound sync now pushes to Lead and/or Contact — whichever has a mapping.\n\n- SfdcOutboundSyncService: pushProfile iterates OUTBOUND_OBJECTS {Lead, Contact};\n  per-object mapping, id property (SFDC_LeadId / SFDC_ContactId — the latter also\n  set by the inbound Contact sync, so round-trips update the same Contact), email\n  match, and per-object create requirements (Lead: LastName+Company; Contact:\n  LastName). Record id written back to the profile for idempotency.\n- SfdcApiClient.findLeadIdByEmail → findSObjectIdByEmail(type, email) (Contact has\n  no IsConverted filter).\n- GetOutboundMappingAction returns Lead + Contact.\n- OutboundMappingTab: Lead/Contact object tabs; per-object required-field hint.\n- en/fr locales: per-object ({{obj}}) mapping messages.\n\nVerified live: one push of pam@luxe.com updated the linked Lead AND created a\nContact (003TE…), 4 fields each; SFDC_ContactId stored back on the profile.\n\n* docs+release: bidirectional README; version 2.0.0","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqYk0cCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGp8QAAlhVRLcvB/boY/w8pMXx3D/\noCQlb4vEZTbw7e8qe9WK6P5UsSIl+/Bx3mIxdsZMia5dTwQ0nXTlhtg/04mJtseN\npqhoO8LpzzKMyYVqz+r2VMkL6Z2ptaEB+NzI8V4CEhEvtN2Sp/Wf4qFw5EfGQX4U\nEF8tLibKFrpe0LxpfwLUkmYScRhR2wXWCna0iUP57galRCyIVh2qwxWI096SnJEK\nOnw4IlB6wwD+nF6Q8r2gJOC0lgTpdH2jZJbqbV7fN4U8CKtMhopNU8Z/GmlHZB/w\n3fOeByzzV3iRnlRS0jEFk0dX4HQYTRoxOTvQmijxBEWvlxJqsWnqshQiplSXtNsV\nmBtMFMeKqwgO/Q8Q61ylrDbpWBoKLrKlTQ+Mv9pN+7Eong5rILpuGzV9mHm1vAk2\n8LnFPmpnhZH1dC9apM/eOH1KVj0cOg44vdIb1JIBRBViWQNp+As9oVfV/gCNRs7n\nd9XOtZwHVPHEHsj6XJPp9OpBZHoiXLd154qOkraoZpBf0i08gZTkdYDwGFWyZekP\nY8yO02C59tGR+6ffSI50/pHbLMPPRjtwd57851k1Gp7mOtLo4TAi+DAq9+xR9mwU\nihmccmrk0dNSvJggQbu9KgzGkE0nudHQTInJbwsJN1PjexYKTlIY2B6j+RuO4pAj\nFY31MkuUMO