api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eemaanamir","id":57627710,"login":"eemaanamir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NjI3NzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/cb937e4646370b43a186a4fcc6b6358f8c3f7b52/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:38:12Z","email":"57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eemaan Amir"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:38:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(dashboards): show sessions scheduled on holidays instead of a static label (#52)\n\nBoth the instructor and trainee HolidaysCard rendered a hard-coded \"No sessions\nscheduled\" subtitle at the card header and ignored the holiday.sessions array\nthe backend already returns. When a holiday overrode the PROTECTED_DATE warning\nand did carry real sessions, the UI falsely claimed the day was clear.\n\nReplace the global subtitle with per-holiday rendering: each row now lists the\nsessions on that day (time · title · course code) and only shows the\n\"No sessions scheduled on this day\" fallback when the array is empty. New\nscoped SCSS classes keep styling out of inline attributes.","tree":{"sha":"240659af1d038448d11320ab5fff2f2fddc36470","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/240659af1d038448d11320ab5fff2f2fddc36470"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/cb937e4646370b43a186a4fcc6b6358f8c3f7b52","verification":{"payload":"tree 240659af1d038448d11320ab5fff2f2fddc36470\nparent 6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0\nauthor Eemaan Amir <57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com> 1791272292 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791272292 +0500\n\nfix(dashboards): show sessions scheduled on holidays instead of a static label (#52)\n\nBoth the instructor and trainee HolidaysCard rendered a hard-coded \"No sessions\nscheduled\" subtitle at the card header and ignored the holiday.sessions array\nthe backend already returns. When a holiday overrode the PROTECTED_DATE warning\nand did carry real sessions, the UI falsely claimed the day was clear.\n\nReplace the global subtitle with per-holiday rendering: each row now lists the\nsessions on that day (time · title · course code) and only shows the\n\"No sessions scheduled on this day\" fallback when the array is empty. New\nscoped SCSS classes keep styling out of inline attributes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxKVkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt70QAIRRCWn4Hs9ybJWYfYqfCcJm\nUk+nxD2ETpwsKCApwXfI3kGipz1pFHk8q3BGdTY1GkCVkS4hYa7U+VIAdSSBN2sh\nd7Wvc2hxZJHBRUP6qNoWvdd/95sVn7OVI4NiLHR2uskfwdzcfWTUg17vnix4rawJ\nbyAX0ZV0v7JWt5J6EoGRI0Qw/sUdX7vSJ67D3xHEogn5KtDnmabwLaQlCD+SBnPT\nni8OCi3QzCu6xQNVDFQ4t6U6N843eXD+HlHF92AcVP2l/PV9yhV4yTIvt/4JmJqF\nvXENqt4bxNfFXu29cX98VAJjPZ6IRecDb6h85Bd49zI9FGN2swdDyPPK8FfeJGnq\naZJuTWlX1IQD7EJASfK7sf9FLxd3a5gNHQ5BFA2Jo9FO9259MirpjRcCgCc4WDVc\nE3a3wrPugMZpI4CS8obynUXF3AmG7Ym4BMNvwsHZNDNCzRbqY1HTHv0Jpab5WckZ\ngRh7mTuSKXCbPsyjagljv6hRiYi7XxW67L/3usvcVUo7Kn4suV2SUVq4Pp+iAwmy\n75u/h4/EvDYC0IZb+MmZEETMocxH2SVkos5Qt7x5xXRsa5bggGJJcofUQQEHe2jl\n6NPwBb9dJK4rYYfyIoubNQrjksI+rc0d43TtAgjqj4YT/WswQYMcw6DGkITfT07s\nWrHailLU1ysh6CFS0iAI\n=AQQY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T07:38:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/cb937e4646370b43a186a4fcc6b6358f8c3f7b52","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKGNiOTM3ZTQ2NDYzNzBiNDNhMTg2YTRmY2M2YjYzNThmOGMzZjdiNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0","sha":"6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0"}],"sha":"cb937e4646370b43a186a4fcc6b6358f8c3f7b52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/cb937e4646370b43a186a4fcc6b6358f8c3f7b52"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:24:05Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T07:24:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(audit log): match the fbr-admin audit log, and use the shared UserIdentity (#51)\n\n* refactor(user identity): use the shared component in place of the local copy\n\nThe requests view rendered a local UserIdentity that duplicated the one\n@edly-io/frontend-component-fbr already exports, along with the 243 lines\nof styling that shipped with it. Both are removed and the import now\npoints at the package.\n\n* fix(modals): open the note, feedback and location dialogs full screen on mobile\n\nThese three dialogs kept their desktop width on a phone, leaving their\ncontent in a narrow column inside the viewport.\n\n* refactor(audit log): bring the dialogs, filters and row actions in line with fbr-admin\n\nThe same audit log ships in three MFEs and had drifted apart. This moves\nthe sessions copy onto the shape fbr-admin settled on.\n\n- the history and change-details dialogs use ModalDialog with a header\n  subtitle, a Paragon DataTable and an ActionRow footer\n- only the table inside a dialog scrolls horizontally, so the title and\n  metadata stay put on a narrow screen\n- the row CTAs are outline buttons rather than bare links\n- the filter row stacks on mobile and lays out from the sm breakpoint up,\n  with the search, action and date controls given explicit widths","tree":{"sha":"bf5416c8d034c1be3cd01ef212d20fabec49bb15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/bf5416c8d034c1be3cd01ef212d20fabec49bb15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0","verification":{"payload":"tree bf5416c8d034c1be3cd01ef212d20fabec49bb15\nparent 2e135922e6006846b7c76c62a5a3632f92d69f67\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1791185045 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791185045 +0500\n\nrefactor(audit log): match the fbr-admin audit log, and use the shared UserIdentity (#51)\n\n* refactor(user identity): use the shared component in place of the local copy\n\nThe requests view rendered a local UserIdentity that duplicated the one\n@edly-io/frontend-component-fbr already exports, along with the 243 lines\nof styling that shipped with it. Both are removed and the import now\npoints at the package.\n\n* fix(modals): open the note, feedback and location dialogs full screen on mobile\n\nThese three dialogs kept their desktop width on a phone, leaving their\ncontent in a narrow column inside the viewport.\n\n* refactor(audit log): bring the dialogs, filters and row actions in line with fbr-admin\n\nThe same audit log ships in three MFEs and had drifted apart. This moves\nthe sessions copy onto the shape fbr-admin settled on.\n\n- the history and change-details dialogs use ModalDialog with a header\n  subtitle, a Paragon DataTable and an ActionRow footer\n- only the table inside a dialog scrolls horizontally, so the title and\n  metadata stay put on a narrow screen\n- the row CTAs are outline buttons rather than bare links\n- the filter row stacks on mobile and lays out from the sm breakpoint up,\n  with the search, action and date controls given explicit widths","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw1CVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeqoQABHV9gDClVUMyMcvLN/fbreP\nhAyh8EqGWYNf40q8tEYe2UURcDMZSNo7Ut8ui5D9ffG/hySXrWMYsL4ndRINBJI1\nM1TaxVwdb0JyIlzGyfLBZnnUF+/f4byPYP0xHZUz1NBmpZkGiW02GPPiVLXRaVYd\n9Nr+7KcIlxn3H9rfYslTb2S85C/5xcMngHCneOeeloZT0wONl9aKAUA4kwS65G/m\nsEdKdCgonqzi35xiiGvO3otiQtAq4EPcfvtN9wzffEp84n0LrieyoLJm1HKbl8iG\nnLA3h3FKMagb0Y0Lygim+LQLM6kvr+1KeYWddPURuwwPN2GCdM3luegydFYJIrUI\nNbAKErQnDvZCzDzGSDWrMZseU9EJPlJPlwVum1GtQkM8a8fmXDP6K1Ut5d6/TMJE\nzThdNcI1lVgZGHaNO5c0+zBPqaFr40fC819SK0NNxCrbq9KeTf4HJ4l7c1CW3WQS\n7Tj88vUv9qTa0x6vcjFPyRpy35Naf534xiEuQRxBMDYCERwPfYgTMbFWHwpoA2N3\n87FMDgLw1OvCuA/oFvpMUiZJ023Nzg6u/A52NYUHeKWmgYoof0RbuRqytZiaqhMo\nYLqt+Zqmo18QfpRTwrzgD4IE1faYO4ql9f2dAwzniZKPiOe4Ioqpim97ALxdqf7N\nsLTkeBUNbrQ5WxEKISwp\n=5SVj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T07:24:06Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKDY2MDFlYjRiMzg1MTUyMWM2ZGMzMjE2YzMyMTEzZjljMTg1OTY2ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/2e135922e6006846b7c76c62a5a3632f92d69f67","sha":"2e135922e6006846b7c76c62a5a3632f92d69f67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/2e135922e6006846b7c76c62a5a3632f92d69f67"}],"sha":"6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/6601eb4b3851521c6dc3216c32113f9c185966d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/2e135922e6006846b7c76c62a5a3632f92d69f67/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:02:32Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:02:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(audit log): use Paragon modals and the shared UserIdentity (#50)\n\nThe audit log built its two dialogs and its actor cell by hand. Both now\nuse the components the rest of the app already uses.\n\nDialogs\n\n- replaces the hand-rolled overlay with Paragon''s StandardModal, which\n  brings a focus trap, focus restore, Escape handling, scroll lock and\n  `aria-modal`\n- the overlay carried `role=\"button\"` and `tabIndex={0}`, so it was\n  announced as a button, and Escape only worked while it held focus; the\n  close control was a bare multiplication sign with no accessible name\n- the change-details dialog was rendered inside the history dialog''s\n  overlay; it is now a sibling\n- each dialog''s table scrolls horizontally inside its own container, so a\n  wide table no longer drags the dialog title and metadata out of view\n\nActor cell\n\n- renders UserIdentity from @edly-io/frontend-component-fbr instead of\n  reproducing its markup, and drops the duplicated styles that shipped\n  with it\n\nAdds tests covering both dialogs, including the stacked case.","tree":{"sha":"b3738879f82105a33961a8a69357a4aaa2989c53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/b3738879f82105a33961a8a69357a4aaa2989c53"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/2e135922e6006846b7c76c62a5a3632f92d69f67","verification":{"payload":"tree b3738879f82105a33961a8a69357a4aaa2989c53\nparent f0077c4f0bde76d83995fb916f37d522651d32f3\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1790942552 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790942552 +0500\n\nrefactor(audit log): use Paragon modals and the shared UserIdentity (#50)\n\nThe audit log built its two dialogs and its actor cell by hand. Both now\nuse the components the rest of the app already uses.\n\nDialogs\n\n- replaces the hand-rolled overlay with Paragon''s StandardModal, which\n  brings a focus trap, focus restore, Escape handling, scroll lock and\n  `aria-modal`\n- the overlay carried `role=\"button\"` and `tabIndex={0}`, so it was\n  announced as a button, and Escape only worked while it held focus; the\n  close control was a bare multiplication sign with no accessible name\n- the change-details dialog was rendered inside the history dialog''s\n  overlay; it is now a sibling\n- each dialog''s table scrolls horizontally inside its own container, so a\n  wide table no longer drags the dialog title and metadata out of view\n\nActor cell\n\n- renders UserIdentity from @edly-io/frontend-component-fbr instead of\n  reproducing its markup, and drops the duplicated styles that shipped\n  with it\n\nAdds tests covering both dialogs, including the stacked case.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv51YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm7oQAF4YE8Xyw5WTu1Tz1mj06m+m\nOrL0Y1etNSFz1ypHzCESl5uKSXlREfZBw8PHtm5xZs7nvJ/QRMrrOqTXzBfahzem\nvyIvN/iqKjbshqiuiT8baa0CgWZWGquhVzoplvjFhcytxSfgNX9RTgniqJkEZIi9\n4XtkgrBDWrqagO6IXfOi5cO6b05oVptmXnnHSxkjuIG/5fmkh11S1aVrSmA1ag+M\nZMfvn8RoYvUZ4qOqeDX0pH2mE/O27GAv3+WXatVSXyYZn61mGqyfKZjpg5KhxjaH\n2nDPgfXAFP0BuM0OAIjobEKx+UF3Vi871uSdYEpdfepXtfeZVZJLuJfEkQkl+fMI\ndn8rWsoPkYdGxpvNJcam/9429RcUW9AmDo2eL6xx2EmPUNhIP5Uzu6aDeoMhltRw\n1tFuL6tgrbb5cyAoGMsJ6OS1H48WMTpEg7YMZCwOAhR6g5u3w0B9ULU4igcrPQRQ\nKJOgiDK/bx+tcST1QilAem3nEZ2h73LVBv6KudrsA+UEeYgGdRF4Horumi92rPaw\nqRgMCD0ntfdPoz5GyukwYbNHEsyCFrTMyCkmyh6NlUv3TrqZZjKOzhrdvMJ1ikgJ\nQa+El+iTz1Z9B+FsW5iDhJggw7/gsO/7r1dna2d0zj0mceYXM8Bgia8ItZ9rLwkp\nl4M+OMq2zo/zkqWtHRFf\n=qzKa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T12:02:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","receiv