,"message":"fix: keep table listings the only horizontally scrolling region\n\nOn a phone the whole page scrolled sideways, pagination included, because\nseveral DataTables rendered bare and their footers propped the layout open\npast the viewport.\n\n- Move DataTable.Table and EmptyTable inside a scroll wrapper on the four\n  request views and on attendance by-learner, leaving TableFooter outside it\n  so only the listing scrolls.\n- Clip horizontal overflow at html/body so nothing but a listing can widen\n  the window; use `clip` rather than `hidden` to keep sticky headers working.\n- Let the table footer wrap and drop the min-content floor on its children.\n- Replace Paragon''s `max-width: 20vw` cell cap with a fixed 20rem, which is\n  ~75px on a phone and cut names and dates off mid-word.\n- Keep the session label and in-cell buttons on one line.","tree":{"sha":"619158554b103148ad88fa9036d0c8df28defbf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/619158554b103148ad88fa9036d0c8df28defbf5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/38ba78eb18ce7479d43ec664b523c9e116cb795e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/38ba78eb18ce7479d43ec664b523c9e116cb795e","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKDM4YmE3OGViMThjZTc0NzlkNDNlYzY2NGI1MjNjOWUxMTZjYjc5NWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/4519f80c2a84fad3845c7149354bf22fbd1582cc","sha":"4519f80c2a84fad3845c7149354bf22fbd1582cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/4519f80c2a84fad3845c7149354bf22fbd1582cc"}],"sha":"38ba78eb18ce7479d43ec664b523c9e116cb795e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/38ba78eb18ce7479d43ec664b523c9e116cb795e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57627710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eemaanamir","id":57627710,"login":"eemaanamir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NjI3NzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/202b66088c5f27381629ad57686c818a8858d0b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:44:45Z","email":"57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eemaan Amir"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:44:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(calendar) + fix(requests): course-scoped instructors, sub badge, wrong sub email, instructor names (#34)\n\n* feat(calendar): scope session instructor dropdown to selected course''s team\n\nPass course_id to the instructors endpoint so only instructors assigned\nto the selected course appear in the scheduling modal (not all city instructors).\nCorrection-mode sessions remain unscoped so past session edits stay unblocked.\n\n* fix(requests): substitute count badge, wrong sub email, and instructor names\n\n- Fix substitute tab badge to count OPEN + ASSIGNED future non-cancelled\n  requests; ASSIGNED rows were silently excluded from the count\n- Fix AssignSubstituteModal to derive the substitute as the first newly-added\n  instructor rather than index [0], which was the original when the admin\n  added a sub without removing the original\n- Show instructor name (email) in the Instructor on Leave and Substitute\n  columns; backend returns submitter_name on nested leave and\n  substitute_instructor_name on the sub request\n- Add \"Sessions scheduled during leave period\" disclaimer to full-day\n  instructor leave rows where sessions fall within the leave window","tree":{"sha":"48124968b8953deced56d9eb64726fdc57fa681f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/48124968b8953deced56d9eb64726fdc57fa681f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/202b66088c5f27381629ad57686c818a8858d0b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 48124968b8953deced56d9eb64726fdc57fa681f\nparent 4519f80c2a84fad3845c7149354bf22fbd1582cc\nauthor Eemaan Amir <57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com> 1789649085 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789649085 +0500\n\nfeat(calendar) + fix(requests): course-scoped instructors, sub badge, wrong sub email, instructor names (#34)\n\n* feat(calendar): scope session instructor dropdown to selected course''s team\n\nPass course_id to the instructors endpoint so only instructors assigned\nto the selected course appear in the scheduling modal (not all city instructors).\nCorrection-mode sessions remain unscoped so past session edits stay unblocked.\n\n* fix(requests): substitute count badge, wrong sub email, and instructor names\n\n- Fix substitute tab badge to count OPEN + ASSIGNED future non-cancelled\n  requests; ASSIGNED rows were silently excluded from the count\n- Fix AssignSubstituteModal to derive the substitute as the first newly-added\n  instructor rather than index [0], which was the original when the admin\n  added a sub without removing the original\n- Show instructor name (email) in the Instructor on Leave and Substitute\n  columns; backend returns submitter_name on nested leave and\n  substitute_instructor_name on the sub request\n- Add \"Sessions scheduled during leave period\" disclaimer to full-day\n  instructor leave rows where sessions fall within the leave window","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq+C9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOlQQAFyN0s8PrOysmJysnc/iPy/x\nUbkawh3oksMO3Bi9ScRxtJaLtwsKMd1fHZ4655s+0SJpyKiNC3S3ath5JwoEdHMD\nGXIbEMtCxE2INh0z9cwG1vb162BlVMfT+kWke0pEmxCHGkRH/11qrnzU8WAq9/4i\nzgbp5rmiMWpihyz0Luv/cKnen9G1uB22ZV1tCqKxCFGSUdvXJYuyTYxyVqheR1qS\nWuBQLGhZFiaAzVBA+9CKACFjsp/YUArTxaoCg3s/O0vg9QFP1xoip7V8fAvdemU2\nFPFTdKrN/TmEmHW8geDq01DWvMAqWimUUhGrCGxnH06psh7Wuwo1V50ukoM0Vx48\nTqFrivLM5mn/xOHB6yrVZxP2cWfJu5dn9b2l0cvrFK8Atus30VlPFe7hgNMY92RV\nL/dF9RSXWiH1emdah6pOGlc1v/WY6VBsQndICFm3y8ZWhtmC9SJGjrmkghtEMCQK\n5PQ0pCFQXg6iFcocjoc/qxOM2406NK0qwuXwOd01Kus1+kFEw5FoI9csi+5ODCmM\nb9qoEOUk5tBVVlCzek8MTYfoozOHRYUGbal9VJy0ivKw5S7ZQxFrbP9fvHscB8HQ\nx03A8AzvNXMKiAQOTzHh22HmM4LM8FxwXUGi1Or3FJ3xaKImhb7h4puALPZQCE6f\n8DpT7+NXreN5ofZbASFs\n=9BPY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verif