ANRVjuR39oMCNlNcfBcAlwW5o2Ax37JSTz7nRQYRvtrJEH5NEFkgIPcKF\nUGNTzMT/UIWKd9LfP9F6NpB/Su60SzF5P1cOrZmro+DeNJAoHmpuPTIA/44hx7jU\nBVpkoOSMgKV1xQdOxODJ/Oj41+z46+5WVh4Mj9KQjqxrdYXHy094wi9uaR3M2TQG\npDmNUtiUG2+nQggrpCuw\n=+aIG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T07:36:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/af4c2451ca5d9083c1b2b45af77bcdf95f46c504","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKGFmNGMyNDUxY2E1ZDkwODNjMWIyYjQ1YWY3N2JjZGY5NWY0NmM1MDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690","sha":"cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130","sha":"06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130"}],"sha":"af4c2451ca5d9083c1b2b45af77bcdf95f46c504","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/af4c2451ca5d9083c1b2b45af77bcdf95f46c504"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:59:31Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:59:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(calendar): move the calendar''s inline styles into its stylesheet (#27) (#28)\n\n* refactor(calendar): move the calendar''s inline styles into its stylesheet\n\nCalendarView carried 80 inline style objects. Thirteen remain, and they are\nthe ones that can only exist at runtime: time-grid geometry (top and height\nfrom the hour scale, left and width from lane percentages), the chip\nbackground from the API''s session-type colour map, the two status colour\nmaps, a minHeight prop, and the line-clamp height computed from block\nheight. Everything else is now a class.\n\nParagon utilities do most of the work rather than new CSS. `text-truncate`\nreplaces the nowrap/hidden/ellipsis trio in eleven places; d-flex,\nalign-items-center, justify-content-center, flex-shrink-0, rounded-circle,\nborder-0, p-0, m-0, w-100, text-left, text-center, text-uppercase, d-block,\noverflow-hidden, overflow-auto, position-absolute, position-relative,\nuser-select-none and the mb/mt spacing steps cover most of the rest. Only\nwhat has no utility equivalent -- gaps, the odd 2/3/5/6/9/11px size, colours,\nshadows -- became SCSS, nested as element and modifier blocks to match\nAuditLogTable.scss and requests.scss.\n\nValues that were computed from a boolean are modifiers now, not styles:\n--today/--weekend/--plain on the day cell, the day name and the time-grid\ncolumn, plus --clickable, --outside, --loading and --divided. The two\ngetCellBackground/getDayHeaderColor helpers collapse into one dayVariant()\nthat returns a modifier suffix.\n\nThree things fell out along the way:\n\n- TitleLink held a useState and four mouse and focus handlers for the sole\n  purpose of swapping its own link colour, with a comment explaining that\n  inline styles cannot express :hover. That is now a :hover, :focus rule, so\n  the state, the handlers and the textStyle object prop are gone; cancelled\n  sessions pass an isCancelled boolean instead.\n- GRADED_DATE_BG/TEXT/BORDER and TIME_COL_WIDTH were JS constants holding\n  CSS values. They live in the stylesheet now.\n- The event title''s line clamp was already broken: stylelint''s\n  value-no-vendor-prefix rule had rewritten `display: -webkit-box` to the\n  inert `display: box`, so `-webkit-line-clamp` did nothing. Rather than\n  reinstate a value the linter strips, the title clamps by\n  max-height: <lines> * 1.25em against its own line-height, landing on whole\n  line boundaries. The trade-off is that a truncated line no longer shows an\n  ellipsis; the full text stays on the element''s title attribute.\n\nNo behaviour change otherwise, and that is measured rather than asserted:\neach block''s original inline declarations were rendered beside the class list\nthat replaced them and the computed styles compared, 351 properties across 78\nblocks, all identical apart from the two display values above. A separate\ncheck confirms every calendar class the JSX uses is defined and every class\ndefined is used.\n\n* refactor(calendar): use Paragon''s Button for the calendar''s link controls\n\nThe session-type info icon, the popover session-title link and the\n\"+N more\" overflow are controls in their own right, so they become\nButton variant=\"link\" rather than hand-rolled <button> elements\ncarrying btn classes. The chips and time-grid blocks are painted\nsurfaces that happen to be clickable, and stay as they are.\n\n.calendar-link-button is compounded with .btn so the restyle outranks\nParagon''s own button rules whichever order the two stylesheets land\nin, and pins display back to a block box: .btn is a centring flex\ncontainer, which would otherwise pull \"+N more\" into the middle of\nits cell.","tree":{"sha":"944beae387a7fbc948fbcdcd687c84b043a4ff45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/944beae387a7fbc948fbcdcd687c84b043a4ff45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690","verification":{"payload":"tree 944beae387a7fbc948fbcdcd687c84b043a4ff45\nparent 218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1788937171 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788937171 +0500\n\nrefactor(calendar): move the calendar''s inline styles into its stylesheet (#27) (#28)\n\n* refactor(calendar): move the calendar''s inline styles into its stylesheet\n\nCalendarView carried 80 inline style objects. Thirteen remain, and they are\nthe ones that can only exist at runtime: time-grid geometry (top and height\nfrom the hour scale, left and width from lane percentages), the chip\nbackground from the API''s session-type colour map, the two status colour\nmaps, a minHeight prop, and the line-clamp height computed from block\nheight. Everything else is now a class.\n\nParagon utilities do most of the work rather than new CSS. `text-truncate`\nreplaces the nowrap/hidden/ellipsis trio in eleven places; d-flex,\nalign-items-center, justify-content-center, flex-shrink-0, rounded-circle,\nborder-0, p-0, m-0, w-100, text-left, text-center, text-uppercase, d-block,\noverflow-hidden, overflow-auto, position-absolute, position-relative,\nuser-select-none and the mb/mt spacing steps cover most of the rest. Only\nwhat has no utility equivalent -- gaps, the odd 2/3/5/6/9/11px size, colours,\nshadows -- became SCSS, nested as element and modifier blocks to match\nAuditLogTable.scss and requests.scss.\n\nValues that were computed from a boolean are modifiers now, not styles:\n--today/--weekend/--plain on the day cell, the day name and the time-grid\ncolumn, plus --clickable, --outside, --loading and --divided. The two\ngetCellBackground/getDayHeaderColor helpers collapse into one dayVariant()\nthat returns a modifier suffix.\n\nThree things fell out along the way:\n\n- TitleLink held a useState and four mouse and focus handlers for the sole\n  purpose of swapping its own link colour, with a comment explaining that\n  inline styles cannot express :hover. That is now a :hover, :focus rule, so\n  the state, the handlers and the textStyle object prop are gone; cancelled\n  sessions pass an isCancelled boolean instead.\n- GRADED_DATE_BG/TEXT/BORDER and TIME_COL_WIDTH were JS constants holding\n  CSS values. They live in the stylesheet now.\n- The event title''s line clamp was already broken: stylelint''s\n  value-no-vendor-prefix rule had rewritten `display: -webkit-box` to the\n  inert `display: box`, so `-webkit-line-clamp` did nothing. Rather than\n  reinstate a value the linter strips, the title clamps by\n  max-height: <lines> * 1.25em against its own line-height, landing on whole\n  line boundaries. The trade-off is that a truncated line no longer shows an\n  ellipsis; the full text stays on the element''s title attribute.\n\nNo behaviour change otherwise, and that is measured rather than asserted:\neach block''s original inline declarations were rendered beside the class list\nthat replaced them and the computed styles compared, 351 properties across 78\nblocks, all identical apart from the two display values above. A separate\ncheck confirms every calendar class the JSX uses is defined and every class\ndefined is used.\n\n* refactor(calendar): use Paragon''s Button for the calendar''s link controls\n\nThe session-type info icon, the popover session-title link and the\n\"+N more\" overflow are controls in their own right, so they become\nButton variant=\"link\" rather than hand-rolled <button> elements\ncarrying btn classes. The chips and time-grid blocks are painted\nsurfaces that happen to be clickable, and stay as they are.\n\n.calendar-link-button is compounded with .btn so the restyle outranks\nParagon''s own button rules whichever order the two stylesheets land\nin, and pins display back to a block box: .btn is a centring flex\ncontainer, which would otherwise pull \"+N more\" into the middle of\nits cell.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoQPTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWssQACUYHar3KdHVE8+kj1ELpz1w\nn5Cr/x0xhNWivp5+jML8fWZvMQj9p60FA7sV8xivBX4EoGaIFxxpLf4B8WkpSAe6\nYh83TNseS7Bh1zaNxQ3TeoUl7u9J+b3VNWo+zHGWGBiDrXYxXzUB4LI34xIjtaph\n92QR3Y7wpi4ESTmeObdsU1i2mSxWlg85MPYh89hzaogbqC8Cy8tU1bG6lLc12X+S\nQYzcQH3nqBQxX9nGLp9Jt0H8YfcPrkmjNPwph/B4ZAyoFxU32HsADlAL48qhHPKf\nJzajavuzxdzuAsjgMbSy+z7JxpVLq3GBHFG4Zo9UbtYU3tLcUEbsR4b28DbulBIT\ni6BDdx5s+eSm6kJI/cgl0GvcbWFrDfX325BH+H64rROK6HcUeKlrewLVxiDrvnx2\ny1IZwTdG2HnIhka0BZWJUiez6gvnzE7+o52V2hzoTeUWCDRoPxEX0xIdoq3cYguX\nB5fQolT7LF7Xhd62w2PS3GMdMlZwaYLwbccIgyX/IP6yxLY7Mui2gyximOpKt2lt\nkskSnlqv2pQ9F4dSHPcel9W+HWgDpjzkFZb5A1jcrM65NHeeDJlMaqOfTfNnvNh4\nwCJhvEzbxoLAhQ1Xqhc4avDIWsAQ6rhsASr1nT1oqznC7+Su4wW0dOzqyecIVwvv\nmw6DSNgbEpzETPrJiXcE\n=gH/b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T06:59:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKGNjODg5MzM0YWYxZTUwNjgwMGViZGZlZjRkMDJlMDYyZjQyMGM2OTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17","sha":"218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17"}],"sha":"cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/cc889334af1e506800ebdfef4d02e062f420c690"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:16:31Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:16:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"style(dashboards): move the dashboard surfaces onto the palette (#25)\n\nThe trainee and instructor dashboards set their page background from\nvar(--pgn-color-bg-light, #F5F6F8). The platform''s dark theme does not define\nthat token, so the literal fallback applied and the page stayed light while\neverything drawn on top of it went dark.\n\nBoth now take the palette''s recessed surface, which is declared in each\nvariant.\n\nTheir pale status pills — the ones carrying dark accent text on a light tint\n— are deliberately left alone for now. They stay readable in dark mode, since\ndark text on a pale fill is still dark text on a pale fill; they just look\nlike bright islands. Moving them onto the palette''s status pairs is a\nfollow-up, and worth doing alongside a look at the two duplicated role-colour\npalettes.","tree":{"sha":"a309ae2a2dc0cb1099b6ec37eca725e1f5970dad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/a309ae2a2dc0cb1099b6ec37eca725e1f5970dad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17","verification":{"payload":"tree a309ae2a2dc0cb1099b6ec37eca725e1f5970dad\nparent f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1788934591 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788934591 +0500\n\nstyle(dashboards): move the dashboard surfaces onto the palette (#25)\n\nThe trainee and instructor dashboards set their page background from\nvar(--pgn-color-bg-light, #F5F6F8). The platform''s dark theme does not define\nthat token, so the literal fallback applied and the page stayed light while\neverything drawn on top of it went dark.\n\nBoth now take the palette''s recessed surface, which is declared in each\nvariant.\n\nTheir pale status pills — the ones carrying dark accent text on a light tint\n— are deliberately left alone for now. They stay readable in dark mode, since\ndark text on a pale fill is still dark text on a pale fill; they just look\nlike bright islands. Moving them onto the palette''s status pairs is a\nfollow-up, and worth doing alongside a look at the two duplicated role-colour\npalettes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoPm/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyREQAIchcANZFQK2OuqyouBsgcFy\njBR8a5vyxCq0oOJgWHnwOHgtT4JuuJi5l/68s4RNkLwPNRp9EknwdNy3K5i+3K4O\nj6o+vE3fiI9Hg+712VuCuI2KFseNE8zZtgMZkI0AcnVuSzfNiAMXPKuwUGLxdDf9\n3sOcP80PKtyGL2u096RJTdbXn8qAWNTVPcqEiMzVgPj6NX96MNadkCkw6m8HphYE\njUg+XjQyqrdIWcsap6KQ//KxEGyI1QNKR2RCNzmO27r1loCTXR3Z2QjRc0r24b+D\nMmEdDbcD0n8dZb85Pd8y1QInfp8Lg/DOM4bJVCsDIJdugHAjS+MC0bOT7c64OEJb\nsMktalyHayi6QMAv1W9Q+ISPDdO3SyUU3vi4O3ocu9Y5yhhs//SibK1I8PStgkNH\n1EMC3zo57Uw6t0cetJN6fQ1WbgpBvcVyUEbS6pO1tmRgp03aCsvqEXV4gRaBnKgh\nhv1uVvTX0WalxtxfSW+Uh9n/RFpjywfguDheAdqZ2Ve/r+TsFMHfxA3dQJ3DpCOU\ndAfJahOlYGGAFj3bwg3yUlJySZxeKzyemlw4gHiPfi2DsdcjUotlU8ga9iZru5/G\nnzvMwsRPEn+8jVjC1k1F9shT4zaqPhEFXrLAFebUudUHfF4H7sMOUc7T7t/pJ6X3\ny0iYVSdz2SwqgqUkypgS\n=6FR/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T06:16:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKDIxOGZkMGNlYTBmY2IyZDYyMWY2OTQxNDdjMDJlMDMwNWQ5MTBhMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b","sha":"f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b"}],"sha":"218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/218fd0cea0fcb2d621f694147c02e0305d910a17"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51116673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/arbirali","id":51116673,"login":"arbirali","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMTE2Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arbirali","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:16:31Z","email":"rahat.ali@arbisoft.com","name":"Rahat Ali"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T06:16:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rahat/responsive UI (#24)\n\n* style: add a theme-aware palette and global field and table rules\n\nThe platform sets data-paragon-theme-variant=\"dark\" on <html> and reloads to\npull in the dark Paragon stylesheet. That flips Paragon''s own tokens but knows\nnothing about colours we hard-code ourselves, so every neutral surface, border\nand text colour of ours has to be declared in both variants or it stays light\non a dark page.\n\nsrc/theme.scss declares that palette. The light values are the ones the app\nalready shipped, so light mode is unchanged; the dark values are anchored on\nthe platform''s dark page background (#0D0D0E) and body text (#CCCCCC) so our\nsurfaces read as sitting just above the page. Brand navy, accent blue and the\nsession/type colours are deliberately absent: they carry meaning and read\ncorrectly on both grounds.\n\nindex.scss also gains:\n\n- One rule that renders form controls at Paragon''s small size below lg and\n  restores the base tokens above it, since Paragon''s size prop takes a single\n  static value and has no responsive form.\n- .sessions-table-scroll, a per-column min-width so a listing scrolls\n  horizontally instead of squeezing five to ten columns into a phone width.\n  The floor is per column rather than per table, so a four-column listing\n  still fits while a ten-column one scrolls.\n- .sessions-section-heading and .sessions-eyebrow, replacing inline styles.\n- A dark-mode override for the role labels, whose light palette falls below\n  3:1 on the dark ground.\n\n* feat(nav): use Paragon Tabs for the section and page tab strips\n\nThe section nav and the four page-level view switchers were hand-rolled\nbutton strips that ran off the side of a narrow screen. Paragon''s Tabs\nalready handles overflow: it measures the strip and moves whatever does not\nfit into a \"More...\" dropdown, so none of that logic needs writing here.\n\nTwo details worth knowing:\n\n- The strip is keyed on the visible section slugs. Paragon measures once on\n  mount, and the role-gated sections arrive from an async config call, so\n  without the key it would keep the measurement it took when four tabs were\n  present and show \"More...\" next to a half-empty row. A regression test\n  covers that case.\n- Paragon marks the active tab from a MutationObserver on aria-selected, so\n  loading straight into an already-overflowed section fires nothing and\n  leaves \"More...\" unmarked. programs.scss restores it with :has() from\n  state already in the DOM.\n\nThe section is read positionally from the path because a programId carries\n\":\" and \"+\", which would need escaping to match against.\n\nsetupTest.js gains a ResizeObserver stub: jsdom has none, and Paragon''s\noverflow hook needs it.\n\n* feat(programs): make the programs and courses pages responsive\n\nMobile-first, driven by Paragon''s breakpoint custom media rather than\ndesktop-first max-width queries, so the desktop layout is what the last\nbreakpoint produces and is unchanged.\n\n- The programs list is a wrapping flex row: one column, then two at sm,\n  three at md, four at xl. Cards in a row keep equal heights, which needed\n  height: auto on the card itself, since its own height: 100% was resolving\n  against the old grid area and defeating stretch.\n- The course card stacks below md and becomes a row above it, with the\n  220x160 thumbnail restored at md.\n- The program header and page content own their horizontal padding, so the\n  Paragon Container inside them has its half-gutter zeroed to stop the two\n  from stacking and shifting the desktop layout.\n- Card surfaces, borders, muted text and the four banner variants move onto\n  the palette, and the cards gain a hairline ring composed into their\n  existing box-shadow, because a shadow does no separating on a dark ground.\n  Composing it into the shadow keeps the box the same size in both variants.\n\nValidated at 320, 375, 576, 768, 992, 1200 and 1400: no horizontal overflow,\nno clipped titles, equal card heights, gaps rendering at the intended 24px.\n\n* feat(requests): rebuild the filters on the Paragon grid\n\nThe filter bars were a single flex row of unlabelled controls with the action\nbuttons mixed in, and the controls stretched to fill whatever width was\navailable. Responsive does not mean width: 100% everywhere, so the widths now\ncome from grid columns instead of overrides.\n\nEach filter row is a Paragon Row of Cols with a label above the control:\nsearch at col-12 col-sm-6 col-lg-3, the selects at col-sm-6 col-md-3\ncol-lg-2, and the submission-date pair at col-sm-auto so it takes only the\nwidth it needs. That yields one row on a desktop, the dates wrapping to a\nsecond row at md, and a clean stack on a phone, where full width is the right\nanswer. The primary and bulk actions moved out of the filter row onto their\nown strip above the table.\n\nA native date input will not shrink below the intrinsic width of its own\nfields, so two side by side overflowed the column on a ~350px screen. Below\nsm the pair stacks, each input carrying a From/To label so the range still\nreads as one control; from sm it is a row of two 10.25rem inputs.\n\nAlso here:\n\n- The hand-rolled table in the leave-usage panel becomes a Paragon DataTable,\n  matching the fifteen other listings in the repo. Its cells are module-level\n  components with propTypes, following the holidays page rather than the\n  audit log''s eslint-disables, and the threshold rides on the row instead of\n  closing over render scope.\n- Every listing gets the horizontal-scroll treatment on small screens.\n- Inline styles give way to SCSS and to Paragon Badge variants for the saved\n  and error states. The amber leave-count keeps its own colour because\n  Paragon''s warning token is a pure yellow that fails on white.\n- Four byte-identical local SectionHeading definitions collapse into one\n  shared component.\n- The create and assign modals get isFullscreenOnMobile.\n\nAPI calls, filter and sort logic, pagination, state and table data are\nuntouched. Validated at 1440, 1200, 992, 768, 576, 414, 390, 375, 360, 350\nand 320: no control needlessly full width on a desktop, nothing escaping its\ncolumn, no viewport overflow.\n\n* feat(shared): responsive audit-log filters, holidays and locations headers\n\nThe audit-log filter bar stacks on a phone and lays out as\nsearch / action / date-range from sm up, with the search band capped rather\nthan stretched. Its controls are Paragon Form.Control with real labels\ninstead of bare inputs.\n\nThe holidays and locations pages stack their heading, description and primary\naction below sm, and their listings pick up the horizontal-scroll treatment.\nThe holidays modal''s hand-rolled info banner becomes a Paragon Alert, which\nalso gains it role=\"alert\".\n\nThe audit modal''s panel and rows, its diff colours and the actor role labels\nmove onto the palette. One latent bug fixed on the way: the actor name\nreferenced --pgn-color-text-base, which this theme does not define, so the\ndeclaration was silently inheriting.\n\n* fix(calendar): align the month grid columns and theme its cells\n\nThe month grid used grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr), and 1fr means\nminmax(auto, 1fr). That auto floor is the item''s min-content width, so a cell\nholding a long session title could not shrink past the chip and took the\nspace from its neighbours. Measured before the fix, on the week carrying two\nevents:\n\n  1440px   198 198 198 202 198 198 198   day numbers up to   2px off\n   768px    73  73  73 202 151  73  73                       73px off\n   375px    38  38  38 202 151  38  38                      230px off\n\nCompounding it, the day-name row was a plain flex row at full width while the\ngrid sat inside 4px of padding with 4px gaps, so the names could never line\nup with the columns even when the columns were equal.\n\nBoth rows now share one geometry: same padding, same gap, and the same\nflex: 0 0 calc((100% - 24px) / 7) column class, with min-width: 0 to remove\nthe intrinsic floor. Flexbox rather than a fixed grid template, matching the\nprograms grid. Below md, seven columns cannot hold a chip at all, so the\nmonth keeps a legible column width and the wrapper scrolls sideways; the\nday-name row scrolls with it because both sit inside the scrolling element.\n\nCell backgrounds, borders, day numbers, the weekday header and the holiday,\ngraded, on-leave and leave-approved chips move onto the palette. The day\nnumber was the clearest symptom of the theming bug: it inherited the theme''s\nbody colour onto a hard-coded white cell, so on a dark page it was white on\nwhite.\n\nAfter: identical columns and zero drift at 1440, 1200, 992, 768, 576, 414,\n375 and 320, chips clipped inside their own cell, columns holding at 96px on\na phone. This also removes the last inline styles from the month view.\n\n* feat(attendance): stack the session card and drop its inline styles\n\nThe session context card kept its status text and the four count badges in\none justify-content-between row, which crowded them on a phone. They now\nstack below sm and sit on one row above it, with the badge row allowed to\nwrap.\n\nThe card''s inline styles are gone. Paragon''s Stack replaces the five\nhand-set flex gaps, its colour utilities replace a hard-coded green and a\nliteral muted grey, and the uppercase COURSE/SESSION labels use a shared\nclass. What Paragon cannot express — the status toggle''s pill shape and equal\nhit area, the toast anchoring, and one absolute type size — lives in a new\nattendance.scss.\n\nThe type size is pinned rather than using Paragon''s .small: that scale is\npercentage-based, so inside this card''s 18px context it resolves to 15.75px\nwhere these lines have always been 14px.\n\nThe grey panel was Bootstrap''s .bg-light, which is a named colour rather than\na themed surface: it stays light on a dark page and drags the theme''s\nby-then-light body text along with it. It now uses the palette''s panel\nsurface.\n\nThe attendance dashboard headings and the summary toggle buttons move onto\nthe palette and out of inline styles at the same time.","tree":{"sha":"8f7d06f1efa364b5d907516936a52daeb240981a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/8f7d06f1efa364b5d907516936a52daeb240981a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f7d06f1efa364b5d907516936a52daeb240981a\nparent 7b0e9f123b48cc54bb263d4a064e3478cfd00f53\nauthor Rahat Ali <rahat.ali@arbisoft.com> 1788934591 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788934591 +0500\n\nRahat/responsive UI (#24)\n\n* style: add a theme-aware palette and global field and table rules\n\nThe platform sets data-paragon-theme-variant=\"dark\" on <html> and reloads to\npull in the dark Paragon stylesheet. That flips Paragon''s own tokens but knows\nnothing about colours we hard-code ourselves, so every neutral surface, border\nand text colour of ours has to be declared in both variants or it stays light\non a dark page.\n\nsrc/theme.scss declares that palette. The light values are the ones the app\nalready shipped, so light mode is unchanged; the dark values are anchored on\nthe platform''s dark page background (#0D0D0E) and body text (#CCCCCC) so our\nsurfaces read as sitting just above the page. Brand navy, accent blue and the\nsession/type colours are deliberately absent: they carry meaning and read\ncorrectly on both grounds.\n\nindex.scss also gains:\n\n- One rule that renders form controls at Paragon''s small size below lg and\n  restores the base tokens above it, since Paragon''s size prop takes a single\n  static value and has no responsive form.\n- .sessions-table-scroll, a per-column min-width so a listing scrolls\n  horizontally instead of squeezing five to ten columns into a phone width.\n  The floor is per column rather than per table, so a four-column listing\n  still fits while a ten-column one scrolls.\n- .sessions-section-heading and .sessions-eyebrow, replacing inline styles.\n- A dark-mode override for the role labels, whose light palette falls below\n  3:1 on the dark ground.\n\n* feat(nav): use Paragon Tabs for the section and page tab strips\n\nThe section nav and the four page-level view switchers were hand-rolled\nbutton strips that ran off the side of a narrow screen. Paragon''s Tabs\nalready handles overflow: it measures the strip and moves whatever does not\nfit into a \"More...\" dropdown, so none of that logic needs writing here.\n\nTwo details worth knowing:\n\n- The strip is keyed on the visible section slugs. Paragon measures once on\n  mount, and the role-gated sections arrive from an async config call, so\n  without the key it would keep the measurement it took when four tabs were\n  present and show \"More...\" next to a half-empty row. A regression test\n  covers that case.\n- Paragon marks the active tab from a MutationObserver on aria-selected, so\n  loading straight into an already-overflowed section fires nothing and\n  leaves \"More...\" unmarked. programs.scss restores it with :has() from\n  state already in the DOM.\n\nThe section is read positionally from the path because a programId carries\n\":\" and \"+\", which would need escaping to match against.\n\nsetupTest.js gains a ResizeObserver stub: jsdom has none, and Paragon''s\noverflow hook needs it.\n\n* feat(programs): make the programs and courses pages responsive\n\nMobile-first, driven by Paragon''s breakpoint custom media rather than\ndesktop-first max-width queries, so the desktop layout is what the last\nbreakpoint produces and is unchanged.\n\n- The programs list is a wrapping flex row: one column, then two at sm,\n  three at md, four at xl. Cards in a row keep equal heights, which needed\n  height: auto on the card itself, since its own height: 100% was resolving\n  against the old grid area and defeating stretch.\n- The course card stacks below md and becomes a row above it, with the\n  220x160 thumbnail restored at md.\n- The program header and page content own their horizontal padding, so the\n  Paragon Container inside them has its half-gutter zeroed to stop the two\n  from stacking and shifting the desktop layout.\n- Card surfaces, borders, muted text and the four banner variants move onto\n  the palette, and the cards gain a hairline ring composed into their\n  existing box-shadow, because a shadow does no separating on a dark ground.\n  Composing it into the shadow keeps the box the same size in both variants.\n\nValidated at 320, 375, 576, 768, 992, 1200 and 1400: no horizontal overflow,\nno clipped titles, equal card heights, gaps rendering at the intended 24px.\n\n* feat(requests): rebuild the filters on the Paragon grid\n\nThe filter bars were a single flex row of unlabelled controls with the action\nbuttons mixed in, and the controls stretched to fill whatever width was\navailable. Responsive does not mean width: 100% everywhere, so the widths now\ncome from grid columns instead of overrides.\n\nEach filter row is a Paragon Row of Cols with a label above the control:\nsearch at col-12 col-sm-6 col-lg-3, the selects at col-sm-6 col-md-3\ncol-lg-2, and the submission-date pair at col-sm-auto so it takes only the\nwidth it needs. That yields one row on a desktop, the dates wrapping to a\nsecond row at md, and a clean stack on a phone, where full width is the right\nanswer. The primary and bulk actions moved out of the filter row onto their\nown strip above the table.\n\nA native date input will not shrink below the intrinsic width of its own\nfields, so two side by side overflowed the column on a ~350px screen. Below\nsm the pair stacks, each input carrying a From/To label so the range still\nreads as one control; from sm it is a row of two 10.25rem inputs.\n\nAlso here:\n\n- The hand-rolled table in the leave-usage panel becomes a Paragon DataTable,\n  matching the fifteen other listings in the repo. Its cells are module-level\n  components with propTypes, following the holidays page rather than the\n  audit log''s eslint-disables, and the threshold rides on the row instead of\n  closing over render scope.\n- Every listing gets the horizontal-scroll treatment on small screens.\n- Inline styles give way to SCSS and to Paragon Badge variants for the saved\n  and error states. The amber leave-count keeps its own colour because\n  Paragon''s warning token is a pure yellow that fails on white.\n- Four byte-identical local SectionHeading definitions collapse into one\n  shared component.\n- The create and assign modals get isFullscreenOnMobile.\n\nAPI calls, filter and sort logic, pagination, state and table data are\nuntouched. Validated at 1440, 1200, 992, 768, 576, 414, 390, 375, 360, 350\nand 320: no control needlessly full width on a desktop, nothing escaping its\ncolumn, no viewport overflow.\n\n* feat(shared): responsive audit-log filters, holidays and locations headers\n\nThe audit-log filter bar stacks on a phone and lays out as\nsearch / action / date-range from sm up, with the search band capped rather\nthan stretched. Its controls are Paragon Form.Control with real labels\ninstead of bare inputs.\n\nThe holidays and locations pages stack their heading, description and primary\naction below sm, and their listings pick up the horizontal-scroll treatment.\nThe holidays modal''s hand-rolled info banner becomes a Paragon Alert, which\nalso gains it role=\"alert\".\n\nThe audit modal''s panel and rows, its diff colours and the actor role labels\nmove onto the palette. One latent bug fixed on the way: the actor name\nreferenced --pgn-color-text-base, which this theme does not define, so the\ndeclaration was silently inheriting.\n\n* fix(calendar): align the month grid columns and theme its cells\n\nThe month grid used grid-template-columns: repeat(7, 1fr), and 1fr means\nminmax(auto, 1fr). That auto floor is the item''s min-content width, so a cell\nholding a long session title could not shrink past the chip and took the\nspace from its neighbours. Measured before the fix, on the week carrying two\nevents:\n\n  1440px   198 198 198 202 198 198 198   day numbers up to   2px off\n   768px    73  73  73 202 151  73  73                       73px off\n   375px    38  38  38 202 151  38  38                      230px off\n\nCompounding it, the day-name row was a plain flex row at full width while the\ngrid sat inside 4px of padding with 4px gaps, so the names could never line\nup with the columns even when the columns were equal.\n\nBoth rows now share one geometry: same padding, same gap, and the same\nflex: 0 0 calc((100% - 24px) / 7) column class, with min-width: 0 to remove\nthe intrinsic floor. Flexbox rather than a fixed grid template, matching the\nprograms grid. Below md, seven columns cannot hold a chip at all, so the\nmonth keeps a legible column width and the wrapper scrolls sideways; the\nday-name row scrolls with it because both sit inside the scrolling element.\n\nCell backgrounds, borders, day numbers, the weekday header and the holiday,\ngraded, on-leave and leave-approved chips move onto the palette. The day\nnumber was the clearest symptom of the theming bug: it inherited the theme''s\nbody colour onto a hard-coded white cell, so on a dark page it was white on\nwhite.\n\nAfter: identical columns and zero drift at 1440, 1200, 992, 768, 576, 414,\n375 and 320, chips clipped inside their own cell, columns holding at 96px on\na phone. This also removes the last inline styles from the month view.\n\n* feat(attendance): stack the session card and drop its inline styles\n\nThe session context card kept its status text and the four count badges in\none justify-content-between row, which crowded them on a phone. They now\nstack below sm and sit on one row above it, with the badge row allowed to\nwrap.\n\nThe card''s inline styles are gone. Paragon''s Stack replaces the five\nhand-set flex gaps, its colour utilities replace a hard-coded green and a\nliteral muted grey, and the uppercase COURSE/SESSION labels use a shared\nclass. What Paragon cannot express — the status toggle''s pill shape and equal\nhit area, the toast anchoring, and one absolute type size — lives in a new\nattendance.scss.\n\nThe type size is pinned rather than using Paragon''s .small: that scale is\npercentage-based, so inside this card''s 18px context it resolves to 15.75px\nwhere these lines have always been 14px.\n\nThe grey panel was Bootstrap''s .bg-light, which is a named colour rather than\na themed surface: it stays light on a dark page and drags the theme''s\nby-then-light body text along with it. It now uses the palette''s panel\nsurface.\n\nThe attendance dashboard headings and the summary toggle buttons move onto\nthe palette and out of inline styles at the same time.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqoPm/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj+wQABu+FYQ34XlJEEPEdiOhdB+U\nMq1i9Q91Zqb/ghT41ILWZFfwGoWfsu9fF1tFP1DR4ZB/dGjHU/nVl6CD1cpSt9LV\n8kOzwCRZ0ozZG2pjV6kQsiWouKR2ee/Yc4nvoJK0g/Yu6ItApkl4aw5yiiYUfMSU\niLJV4X9UCwz4vTgMDSHMTEKnGimNBUechz50ri9zW6LSpygPsNhmDjUUcIzbdbUE\n5lgsiFJ3TbyFyApGKenGAZoOgiX+NQ+LRO0V99W9Etcvv5V6Z4aaGQPXdbx+OlHr\nMU2bxpz2/UW6QNF178BLdS+lIMwla7dcY9NJnEaB7bjtwCZyPNNpZGAc7nlRmob0\n11WzLQtLH65Y1hOfMrDlYfPm94y1lZ+7NRpJvyYmHNJaXU7RjNlCHg+3N/WUNI53\nXow7npT71ULaj2zX02exy+an3FxL2Vzhglj9QMProLKN/vn8DWo+8yQAhDAhqhgT\nJQGuJqxnR0Ys8EeqXGOunoqUZE8zEyDq5XcnLSxJI9q9u4g0wPWJ9KgqWLXrm9Fz\nlOuuX2WBo4G69fkaMRCMiNd6jJjSiC7U1zCCXro0WcvroHEfWxxIzxlQxR7DjPoD\nCB2x8soEMZCtUomLFulrAkBgJQ2miNyGt0VXPqoQRvy3eFjZJEcyF2VjGr4Ng1Ia\nP/6g/s3puBIWNBQE/efh\n=JdQE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T06:16:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKGYzNTdmNzk2ODk2ZGJiNDRjYzJjMGYwNzZjZjliMjliM2UzMjk4NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/7b0e9f123b48cc54bb263d4a064e3478cfd00f53","sha":"7b0e9f123b48cc54bb263d4a064e3478cfd00f53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/7b0e9f123b48cc54bb263d4a064e3478cfd00f53"}],"sha":"f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/f357f796896dbb44cc2c0f076cf9b29b3e32984b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260585696?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muhammadammar-ma","id":260585696,"login":"muhammadammar-ma","node_id":"U_kgDOD4g44A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:12:06Z","email":"muhammad.ammar@arbisoft.com","name":"Muhammad Ammar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:12:06Z","email":"muhammad.ammar@arbisoft.com","name":"Muhammad Ammar"},"message":"feat(attendance): hide the Zoom sync button outside the sync window\n\nThe \"Sync attendance from Zoom\" button showed whenever an admin viewed a\nsession with a meeting_id — including before the meeting ended and after\nthe marking window closed, where the backend now returns 400. Gate the\nbutton on the same bounds (ended session, meeting present, window open)\nso the UI matches the endpoint. Adds the roster page''s first test file.","tree":{"sha":"9339906a73b9ee1f47b7af0c6122340106c91b0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/9339906a73b9ee1f47b7af0c6122340106c91b0e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260585696?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/muhammadammar-ma","id":260585696,"login":"muhammadammar-ma","node_id":"U_kgDOD4g44A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muhammadammar-ma","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130","node_id":"C_kwDOSw9BL9oAKDA2Zjk3NWMwMGNhYjAzM2Y5ZDY1NzdmYjFkZDUyN2M4N2M1ZjAxMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commit/33e39404042d5dbf3fa4805323c7761f3237e300","sha":"33e39404042d5dbf3fa4805323c7761f3237e300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/33e39404042d5dbf3fa4805323c7761f3237e300"}],"sha":"06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/06f975c00cab033f9d6577fb1dd527c87c5f0130"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57627710?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/eemaanamir","id":57627710,"login":"eemaanamir","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NjI3NzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eemaanamir","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/commits/7b0e9f123b48cc54bb263d4a064e3478cfd00f53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T08:15:42Z","email":"57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Eemaan Amir"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T08:15:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(programs): clear false Refine badge on initial load (#22)\n\nThe sort default was evaluated before config loaded (isAdmin was false),\nso sortOrder initialised to ''enrolled''. Once config resolved and isAdmin\nbecame true the defaultSort flipped to ''az'', making the badge count\n''enrolled !== az'' as 1 even though the user had not touched the filter.\n\nFix: initialise sortOrder to '''' and resolve it against the real\ndefaultSort in a useEffect that fires once config is available.","tree":{"sha":"48e45c925fed27bd1b222798b1a69fb07dcde9c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/trees/48e45c925fed27bd1b222798b1a69fb07dcde9c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/edly-io/frontend-app-sessions/git/commits/7b0e9f123b48cc54bb263d4a064e3478cfd00f53","verification":{"payload":"tree 48e45c925fed27bd1b222798b1a69fb07dcde9c4\nparent 33e39404042d5dbf3fa4805323c7761f3237e300\nauthor Eemaan Amir <57627710+eemaanamir@users.noreply.github.com> 1788855342 +0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788855342 +0500\n\nfix(programs): clear false Refine badge on initial load (#22)\n\nThe sort default was evaluated before config loaded (isAdmin was false),\nso sortOrder initialised to ''enrolled''. Once config resolved and isAdmin\nbecame true the defaultSort flipped to ''az'', making the badge count\n''enrolled !== az'' as 1 even though the user had not touched the filter.\n\nFix: initialise sortOrder to '''' and resolve it against the real\ndefaultSort in a useEffect that fires once config is available.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqn8QuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJfEQACkhD6CQ/mN3VRTp/tD4dzX3\ngusSPWFlQ1LFk0MoJicrRS7Ys6w0s4q2vFxDftue6JfHGHzIFYvxKSUJ4JgyCztB\nNLUft7kwoJf3l/DdcKGhaul30Vbs8li325oqNMUc/o6G1wj2PyhIpbE3FAh/S8f5\nrfmCxYm5alAkRCztQ/gs+Z82O1d8tRf5b+MejtQXHgsuFGutOn2DPSG5OnzvCS34\nMJnRJcRCjWOxZG1qHInYVVBqE2uG2bRGnJE5rLXx+gvZ4IQYSSUC7eWPm0tohqS5\ngWVeMmorg0p/5rIHOjS/mTbZ/BLLqtYRuErYRrZWcPTTSRfaGIn+XVJNDYNAups/\nbyMGI2NFGLSXWcLE0kisluo1dNxJ8oUJLjCXnjsMm+KJGw1uu5m71+QbuMa4abWf\nNjFauy0tBjdNPqniC7ND1zyP+KiUAt65qAoykwhE5sSQr/OixTIm2mWJ3G75AscT\nyz9cmZ1NoHS4hcn8NVUxySXkKBkQsa5eiejXmtlJR3I+A