2e44ee0dfbf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-06T07:24:01Z","email":"claytonjcody@gmail.com","name":"Cody Clayton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-06T07:24:01Z","email":"claytonjcody@gmail.com","name":"Cody Clayton"},"message":"feat(infra): Deploy-2 federation host portal.st6weeklycommit.com — S3+CloudFront+ACM+Route53 (authored, NOT applied)\n\nStand up the Module-Federation HOST origin (portal.<ROOT_DOMAIN>) ahead of Deploy 2,\nisolated in a self-contained infra/terraform/portal.tf so it never entangles the\npolish / clean-green deploys.\n\n- portal.tf mirrors the wc. SPA hosting (s3_cloudfront.tf): private S3 + OAC +\n  CloudFront + SPA fallback (403/404 -> index.html), alias portal.<ROOT_DOMAIN>,\n  OAC-scoped bucket policy. Reuses the module-global data sources.\n- SEPARATE us-east-1 ACM cert for portal.<ROOT_DOMAIN> kept HERE (not route53_acm.tf),\n  so a portal cert (re)validation never touches the live wc./api. certs — the\n  cert-revalidation-off-the-clean-green-runs concern stays satisfied.\n- Route53 portal.<ROOT_DOMAIN> A-alias -> portal CloudFront + the DNS-validation\n  CNAME records (canonical ACM for_each pattern).\n- outputs.tf: s3_portal_bucket_name + portal_cloudfront_distribution_id (CI\n  sync/invalidation targets) + portal_cert_arn.\n\nAgent-side gate green: terraform fmt -check + validate + tflint all rc=0. NOT\napplied — Deploy 2 only (lead-assembled, separate from the polish deploy). The\nremote-publish/CORS choice + the deploy.yml host/remote build steps are the\nfrontend-coupled next pieces (see the report).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"40556c68dcb5d1f5907e28d9c421e45797e4b1c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SiWarlock/st6-weekly-commit/git/trees/40556c68dcb5d1f5907e28d9c421e45797e4b1c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SiWarlock/st6-weekly-commit/git/commits/fffafe93118a6247ee971bf74d062e44ee0dfbf4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsi