":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SiWarlock/st6-weekly-commit/commits/9e5a5d91f37d527fe05e3776b19ca5cabed5f9a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-04T15:05:31Z","email":"claytonjcody@gmail.com","name":"Cody Clayton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-04T15:05:31Z","email":"claytonjcody@gmail.com","name":"Cody Clayton"},"message":"fix(wc-api): worker boots DB-less in the aws profile (JPA exclude + profile rename) (092)\n\nThe deployed wc-sync-worker would crashloop in aws: :shared carries the\ndata-jpa starter (task 1.5), which transitively activates\nDataSourceAutoConfiguration + HibernateJpaAutoConfiguration in the worker,\nbut the worker mounts graph-only secrets (no spring.datasource.*) ->\n\"Failed to determine a suitable driver class\". The exclude existed only as a\ntest-only @SpringBootTest property, so the production gap was invisible\n(finding from the 091 boot-smoke).\n\nExclude both auto-configs in production on WcSyncWorkerApplication (the\nworker is DB-less in every Wave-1 profile; Wave-2''s SQS consumer removes the\nexclude + wires the datasource). Drop the now-redundant test-only exclude\nproperty — the boot tests prove the production exclude alone keeps the boot\nDB-less, pinned structurally by a no-DataSource / no-EntityManagerFactory\nbean-absence test under @ActiveProfiles(aws).\n\nAlso rename the worker''s application-prod.yml -> application-aws.yml: it was\ndead under SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=aws (the same §42 bug the api fixed at\n090). WorkerFlywayPropertyTest now pins the aws profile (flyway stays off)\n+ that application-aws.yml loads under aws (its logging marker resolves).\n\nUnblocks the deployed worker rollout going Ready on the first deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5487309a60c1669d66cc1e8084818bd5fbaeb65d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SiWarlock/st6-weekly-commit/git/trees/5487309a60c1669d66cc1e8084818bd5fbaeb65d"},"url":"ht