rs.githubusercontent.com/u/1966339?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/cdgutierrez6","id":1966339,"login":"cdgutierrez6","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjYzMzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cdgutierrez6","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdgutierrez6/fleetvision/commits/f597a784bef2ede1a6a7397f64f260f2beeb050e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T07:58:04Z","email":"cdgutierrez6@gmail.com","name":"Cristian Daniel Gutiérrez S."},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T07:58:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(ci): stop *.API.Tests from tanking the coverage gate; billing Application coverage (#10)\n\nThe >=70% quality gate in _ci-dotnet.yml takes the MIN line-rate across every emitted\nCobertura file, and coverage.runsettings filters instrumentation to the Domain/Application\nlayers. billing is the only service with an *.API.Tests project, and its API tests -- scored\nagainst a Domain/Application filter they don''t exercise -- reported ~5% and failed the gate by\nconstruction, no matter how well-covered Domain/Application actually were.\n\nFix (shared, repo-wide): the Test step now emits coverage ONLY for *.Domain.Tests and\n*.Application.Tests. Other test projects (currently just billing''s *.API.Tests) STILL RUN --\na failing API test still fails the build -- they simply don''t emit a gate-tanking Cobertura.\nThis encodes the convention every other service already follows (Domain+Application are the\ngated layers) into the mechanism, instead of relying on nobody ever adding an API.Tests to\ntest-paths. No test stops executing; all green services stay green (they have only\nDomain/Application test projects).\n\nbilling Application tests (the real coverage gap, Group B / #4): Cancel/CreateCheckoutSession\nhandlers, CreateCheckoutSessionCommandValidator, GetBillingPortalUrl/GetSubscription queries,\nplus a cross-tenant isolation test on GetSubscription (handler-level WHERE TenantId== filter,\nindependent of Postgres RLS which EF InMemory can''t enforce). Local: Domain 87.3% / Application\n95.5% -> gate worst 87.3% PASSED. Domain 9 + Application 35 + API 7 tests green.\n\nAlso fixes CS1503 in ValidationExceptionMiddlewareTests: NoActiveStripeSubscription and\nSubscriptionAlreadyCanceled take a Guid, not a string. Reworked to construct with a known\ntenant Guid and assert that Guid never appears in the client response -- the real\nnon-disclosure invariant, not a vacuous literal check.\n\nRefs #4.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cristian Gutierrez <efiziai.notificaciones@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"52d14b2f1c78b468dd951dc3e10616bda917d682","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdgutierrez6/fleetvision/git/trees/52d14b2f1c78b468dd951dc3e10616bda917d682"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cdgutierrez6/fleetvision/git/commits/f597a784bef2ede1a6a7397f64f260f2beeb050e","verification":{"payload":"tree 52d14b2f1c78b468dd951dc3e10616bda917d682\nparent da3d08b080b7f08e6e31bdb84e80d1075a7fadb7\nauthor Cristian Daniel Gutiérrez S. <cdgutierrez6@gmail.com> 1789027084 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789027084 -0500\n\nfix(ci): stop *.API.Tests from tanking the coverage gate; billing Application coverage (#10)\n\nThe >=70% quality gate in _ci-dotnet.yml takes the MIN line-rate across every emitted\nCobertura file, and coverage.runsettings filters instrumentation to the Domain/Application\nlayers. billing is the only service with an *.API.Tests project, and its API tests -- scored\nagainst a Domain/Application filter they don''t exercise -- reported ~5% and failed the gate by\nconstruction, no matter how well-covered Domain/Application actually were.\n\nFix (shared, repo-wide): the Test step now emits coverage ONLY for *.Domain.Tests and\n*.Application.Tests. Other test projects (currently just billing''s *.API.Tests) STILL RUN --\na failing API test still fails the build -- they simply don''t emit a gate-tanking Cobertura.\nThis encodes the convention every other service already follows (Domain+Application are the\ngated layers) into the mechanism, instead of relying on nobody ever adding an API.Tests to\ntest-paths. No test stops executing; all green services stay green (they have only\nDomain/Application test projects).\n\nbilling Application tests (the real coverage gap, Group B / #4): Cancel/CreateCheckoutSession\nhandlers, CreateCheckoutSessionCommandValidator, GetBillingPortalUrl/GetSubscription queries,\nplus a cross-tenant isolation test on GetSubscription (handler-level WHERE TenantId== filter,\nindependent of Postgres RLS which EF InMemory can''t enforce). Local: Domain 87.3% / Application\n95.5% -> gate worst 87.3% PASSED. Domain 9 + Application 35 + API 7 tests green.\n\nAlso fixes CS1503 in ValidationExceptionMiddlewareTests: NoActiveStripeSubscription and\nSubscriptionAlreadyCanceled take a Guid, not a string. Reworked to construct with a known\ntenant Guid and assert that Guid never appears in the client response -- the real\nnon-disclosure invariant, not a vacuous literal check.\n\nRefs #4.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cristian Gutierrez <efiziai.notificaciones@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","sig