rgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/commits/597111d7d893ca28d08cccf2f1ddd81fa617dafe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T21:14:33Z","email":"agent@replit.com","name":"Replit Agent"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T21:14:33Z","email":"agent@replit.com","name":"Replit Agent"},"message":"Fix recent-turns leak, keyless web search, multi-provider image gen\n\nThree-part task on the SiraGPT backend:\n\n1. \"[Recent user turns]\" leak: the conversation-memory filter module declares\n   enabled:false (its extraContext fold once leaked into the visible prompt),\n   but FILTERS_CONFIG hard-overrode it to true. Set the registry default to\n   false to match the module intent (belt-and-suspenders with the prior ai.js\n   extraContext-fold removal).\n\n2. Keyless web search for all models: free-tier fallback made injectable.\n   web-search-tools freeTierSearch accepts opts.freeSearch; searchFreshContext\n   gated by opts.disableFreeTier; gateway-adapter enrichWithWebSearch forwards\n   both.\n\n3. Multi-provider image generation: added 3 fal.ai IMAGE models + provider\n   ''Fal'' to the manifest, exported DEFAULT_ACTIVE_IMAGE_MODEL_NAMES (curated\n   active set across OpenAI/Gemini/OpenRouter/Fal). ai.js gains generateFalImage\n   + falImageSizeFor + a Fal branch in generateSingleImage; Fal edits redirect\n   to Gemini/OpenAI. model-sync seeds curated models active on create.\n\nDeviation from plan (architect review): the curated-IMAGE force-reactivation\noriginally ran on every /models read and /generate-image call, silently\noverriding admin deactivations. Gated it behind a per-instance\n_curatedImageActivationDone flag so it runs once per process (prod singleton)\nwhile tests on fresh instances still exercise it. Kept the curated allow-list\nin the picker/generate gate intentionally (curateVisibleAdminMediaModels must\nnever surface broken picker entries); the curated set already spans all\nimage-capable providers.\n\nConcurrency fix (production P2002): ensureStaticCatalogModels does findMany then\ncreate; on the hot path (/ai/models, /admin/models/sync) two requests race to\ncreate the same row and the loser threw a P2002 unique-constraint error, 500ing\n\"Get models\". Wrapped create in try/catch — on P2002 fall back to a metadata\nupdate without isActive (preserve admin state); rethrow other errors.\n\nTests: updated model-admin-image-catalog (fal models + activation semantics,\nplus P2002 race + non-P2002 propagation cases) and filters-pipeline; wired\norchestration-web-search, orchestration-gateway-adapter, filters-pipeline, and\nmodel-admin-image-catalog into the backend CI test string. Workflow boots clean.","tree":{"sha":"0b8aca80a14936640da6af063a786fecc085a07f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/git/trees/0b8aca80a14936640da6af063a786fecc085a07f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/git/commits/597111d7d893ca28d08cccf2f1ddd81fa617dafe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/207944715?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/replit-agent","id":207944715,"login":"replit-agent","node_id":"U_kgDODGT8Cw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/replit-agent","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/nilsenm/siraGPT/commit/597111d7d893ca28d08cccf2f1ddd81fa617dafe","node_id":"C_kwDOSxaPaNoAKDU5NzExMWQ3ZDg5M2NhMjhkMDhjY2NmMmYxZGRkODFmYTYxN2RhZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nilsenm/siraGPT/commit/1ee1f9051151dcd1247e9cf016fadd8350198a21","sha":"1ee1f9051151dcd1247e9cf016fadd8350198a21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/commits/1ee1f9051151dcd1247e9cf016fadd8350198a21"}],"sha":"597111d7d893ca28d08cccf2f1ddd81fa617dafe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/commits/597111d7d893ca28d08cccf2f1ddd81fa617dafe"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/commits/1ee1f9051151dcd1247e9cf016fadd8350198a21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-03T21:11:27Z","email":"51958395-infosiragpt@users.noreply.replit.com","name":"infosiragpt"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-03T21:11:27Z","email":"51958395-infosiragpt@users.noreply.replit.com","name":"infosiragpt"},"message":"Add health-check test to sharded CI test list\n\nTask #40: Make sure the health-check tests actually run in our automated checks.\n\nProblem: backend/scripts/test-shard.sh builds its CI test-file list by\nextracting tests/*.test.js paths from the `test` script string in\nbackend/package.json. The core health-check unit test\ntests/sira-health-and-metrics.test.js was missing from that string and\nonly appeared in the stale, commented-out legacy job block in\n.github/workflows/ci.yml — so the sharded CI job was not running it and a\nregression in the health/metrics probes could slip through.\n\nChange:\n- Appended tests/sira-health-and-metrics.test.js to the `test` script in\n  backend/package.json (the single source of truth for the sharded run).\n  It was the only health/metric-named file present in the commented-out\n  block but absent from the test script.\n\nVerification:\n- Direct run: `node --test tests/sira-health-and-metrics.test.js` → 41/41 pass.\n- Shard extraction confirmed: file is now picked up by test-shard.sh\n  (count 265 → 266). Targeted slice `bash scripts/test-shard.sh 266 266`\n  runs exactly this file → 41/41 pass.\n- Full `bash scripts/test-shard.sh 1 1` runs all 266 files serially and\n  exceeds the 2-min shell limit (wall-clock only, not a failure); CI runs\n  it across 4 parallel shards.\n\nDeviation: Left the commented-out legacy job block in ci.yml in place.\nIts inline comment explicitly preserves it for fast rollback if sharding\nmisbehaves, and removing it is outside this task''s health-check scope.\nNote: that block references ~111 other test files not in the test script\n— surfaced as a follow-up.\n\nReplit-Task-Id: 66034f3a-e072-4cb1-af0d-e0fc3a52e4c4","tree":{"sha":"024e4fe5c3d1e2c7cfa9c1e4dd896918dfccb3cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/git/trees/024e4fe5c3d1e2c7cfa9c1e4dd896918dfccb3cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/git/commits/1ee1f9051151dcd1247e9cf016fadd8350198a21","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/nilsenm/siraGPT/commit/1ee1f9051151dcd1247e9cf016fadd8350198a21","node_id":"C_kwDOSxaPaNoAKDFlZTFmOTA1MTE1MWRjZDEyNDdlOWNmMDE2ZmFkZDgzNTAxOThhMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/nilsenm/siraGPT/commit/e7844bf075680f40c780cef465447b438a819fc3","sha":"e7844bf075680f40c780cef465447b438a819fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nilsenm/siraGPT/commits/e7844bf0