c143b364928069a411a32cbbc02b0d0","node_id":"C_kwDOSxa_e9oAKDJkMDA4MjY1YWMxNDNiMzY0OTI4MDY5YTQxMWEzMmNiYmMwMmIwZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/threadwick-hq/studio/commit/ce567ba8973a919a7a4e5f4b9ccccb0bc180be2c","sha":"ce567ba8973a919a7a4e5f4b9ccccb0bc180be2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/threadwick-hq/studio/commits/ce567ba8973a919a7a4e5f4b9ccccb0bc180be2c"}],"sha":"2d008265ac143b364928069a411a32cbbc02b0d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/threadwick-hq/studio/commits/2d008265ac143b364928069a411a32cbbc02b0d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/threadwick-hq/studio/commits/ce567ba8973a919a7a4e5f4b9ccccb0bc180be2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:45:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-10T22:45:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Stitch endpoint handles: body moves, head/base dots drag the endpoints\n\nA selected stitch''s base/head dots become drag handles: the head handle\nre-points the head (base pinned, length + rotation recompute), the base\nhandle moves the base (head pinned). Chains are fixed-size, so either\nhandle rotates them — around the pinned base or the pinned head — and\nonly a body drag translates one; the chain body hit area is now its\nfilled oval. Slip stitches are a single point and keep moving as a\nwhole. Handle gestures coalesce into one undo entry (store.adjustStitch,\nunit-tested) and de-automate chains like body drags do.\n\nRefs #40\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BZsB2zJDTUc3nMM2KzfWsY","tree":{"sha":"8d99b3c511a6e4cd42124c76e2e80ddbd574b6c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/threadwick-hq/studio/git/trees/8d99b3c511a6e4cd42124c76e2e80ddbd574b6c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/threadwick-hq/studio/git/commits/ce567ba8973a919a7a4e5f4b9ccccb0bc180be2c","verification":{"payload":"tree 8d99b3c511a6e4cd42124c76e2e80ddbd574b6c2\nparent eb6234fe24e51e340f035975f26d5856dcbfb5e8\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781131519 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1781131519 +0000\n\nStitch endpoint handles: body moves, head/base dots drag the endpoints\n\nA selected stitch''s base/head dots become drag handles: the head handle\nre-points the head (base pinned, length + rotation recompute), the base\nhandle moves the base (head pinned). Chains are fixed-size, so either\nhandle rotates them — around the pinned base or the pinned head — and\nonly a body drag translates one; the chain body hit area is now its\nfilled oval. Slip stitches are a single point and keep moving as a\nwhole. Handle gestures coalesce into one undo entry (store.adjustStitch,\nunit-tested) and de-automate chains like body drags do.\n\nRefs #40\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01BZsB2zJDTUc3nMM2KzfWsY\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNz1PY3O\nqVh8iNt2RrD7WIPMirkMXfxlEUlbp+3AEjszctdZwfzeDyO5bxpso3WxlJ/I1