94e0d8e87561719837d023c2e8bfb4c2e6"}],"sha":"f8cda1b275c9158b3ab073dfeb7ac1a34ac20caa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/2heal1/divebell/commits/f8cda1b275c9158b3ab073dfeb7ac1a34ac20caa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41466093?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/2heal1","id":41466093,"login":"2heal1","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNDY2MDkz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/2heal1","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/2heal1/divebell/commits/3042f294e0d8e87561719837d023c2e8bfb4c2e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T04:03:09Z","email":"TwoHeal@163.com","name":"Hanric"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T04:03:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): support Node 20 runtime (#149)\n\n* feat(cli): support Node 20 runtime\n\nCo-authored-by: TRAE CLI <noreply@bytedance.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): sync agent-browser version in recording skill manifest\n\nPR #149 upgraded @divebell/agent-browser from 0.33.2-divebell.3 to\n0.33.2-divebell.4 in packages/cli/package.json to enable Node 20 support,\nbut the recording skill runtime manifest was left behind.\n\nResult: the Build/Verify recording skill runtime steps packed the\nolder .3 registry tarball while the workspace CLI required .4, causing\ndependency resolution failures in the ''verify-recording-skill-runtime''\nCI stage and failing the entire check job.\n\nSync both specifier and file name in divebell-cli-runtime.json so the\nproduced runtime archive is internally consistent.\n\n* ci(node20): run npm install in clean sandbox with debug output\n\nThe `node20-runtime` job was running `npm install --global` inside\nthe monorepo root, where `.npmrc` contains strict pnpm-oriented\nsettings (engine-strict, strict-peer-dependencies, ...). Under Node 20\nthose settings can abort the global install of the packed CLI tarball,\neven though the CLI and all of its published dependencies\n(@divebell/agent-browser >=0.33.2-divebell.4, @divebell/bridge,\n@divebell/core) declare Node >=20.19 support.\n\nRun the install step inside an isolated temporary directory with a\nblank `.npmrc`, add `--no-audit --no-fund`, and capture the\nstdout/stderr of `npm install` and `divebell setup` separately so\nthe CI annotations surface the real failure point instead of the\ngeneric \"Process completed with exit code 1\".\n\n* fix(cli): shorten setup session names to avoid Unix socket path limit\n\nLinux enforces a hard 108-byte limit on Unix domain socket paths.\n`divebell setup` builds the agent-browser socket path from\n`AGENT_BROWSER_SOCKET_DIR` + a session name like\n`divebell-setup-<uuid>-existing`. On GitHub Actions runners\nunder `$TMPDIR` this produced paths around 116 bytes, failing with\n\"Socket path would be 116 bytes (max 103)\".\n\nShorten the session prefix from `divebell-setup-` to `ds-` (saves\n12 chars) and use one-letter directory names (`h`, `s`, `p`)\nin the node20-runtime CI job for the home, socket, and prefix\npaths so the full socket path stays well under the kernel limit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: TRAE CLI <noreply@bytedance.com>","tree":{"sha":"3afe2b4397f8f5d18222ecfa276c374471dec2d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/2heal1/divebell/git/trees/3afe2b4397f8f5d18222ecfa276c374471dec2d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/2heal1/divebell/git/commits/3042f294e0d8e87561719837d023c2e8bfb4c2e6","verification":{"payload":"tree 3afe2b4397f8f5d18222ecfa276c374471dec2d0\nparent d03ff7950116e0aa20e398bce1169ac65de946f8\nauthor Hanric <TwoHeal@163.com> 1786075389 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786075389 +0800\n\nfeat(cli): support Node 20 runtime (#149)\n\n* feat(cli): support Node 20 runtime\n\nCo-authored-by: TRAE CLI <noreply@bytedance.com>\n\n* fix(runtime): sync agent-browser version in recording skill manifest\n\nPR #149 upgraded @divebell/agent-browser from 0.33.2-divebell.3 to\n0.33.2-divebell.4 in packages/cli/package.json to enable Node 20 support,\nbut the recording skill runtime manifest was left behind.\n\nResult: the Build/Verify recording skill runtime steps packed the\nolder .3 registry tarball while the workspace CLI required .4, causing\ndependency resolution failures in the ''verify-recording-skill-runtime''\nCI stage and failing the entire check job.\n\nSync both specifier and file name in divebell-cli-runtime.json so the\nproduced runtime archive is internally consistent.\n\n* ci(node20): run npm install in clean sandbox with debug output\n\nThe `node20-runtime` job was running `npm install --global` inside\nthe monorepo root, where `.npmrc` contains strict pnpm-oriented\nsettings (engine-strict, strict-peer-dependencies, ...). Under Node 20\nthose settings can abort the global install of the packed CLI tarball,\neven though the CLI and all of its published dependencies\n(@divebell/agent-browser >=0.33.2-divebell.4, @divebell/bridge,\n@divebell/core) declare Node >=20.19 support.\n\nRun the install step inside an isolated temporary directory with a\nblank `.npmrc`, add `--no-audit --no-fund`, and capture the\nstdout/stderr of `npm install` and `divebell setup` separately so\nthe CI annotations surface the real failure point instead of the\ngeneric \"Process completed with exit code 1\".\n\n* fix(cli): shorten setup session names to avoid Unix socket path limit\n\nLinux enforces a hard 108-byte limit on Unix domain socket paths.\n`divebell setup` builds the agent-browser socket path from\n`AGENT_BROWSER_SOCKET_DIR` + a session name like\n`divebell-setup-<uuid>-existing`. On GitHub Actions runners\nunder `$TMPDIR` this produced paths around 116 bytes, failing with\n\"Socket path would be 116 bytes (max 103)\".\n\nShorten the session prefix from `divebell-setup-` to `ds-` (saves\n12 chars) and use one-letter directory names (`h`, `s`, `p`)\nin the node20-runtime CI job for the home, socket, and prefix\npaths so the full socket path stays well under the kernel limit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: TRAE CLI <noreply@bytedance.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqdVj9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQKYQAJt1ZUNUbZjH0EGEpx+deR/k\n2TKd2JmVl17whYE7srlWe4CIm/SeCIoDh3uMCDQolVjveyzD/HfyeJ/YqBqKx/pl\nM9QRj+t5rWlT3tMC6lmF3y8nHoNDKqtED5iYQMkD/LtpFH7hnKFqfrzUao3UDAPD\nwtapx01g8XwgN5IO+Eg/GSVsk8Dx/lbS5rcoO+xHCDH5QDovzn1Jp0fNKEY3pgEP\nNgGH8gpzHE7HbCrMgp5VJIzRldD5T57Pn5a4cmxiIY0eEFAQMN1N6qzZipb2bptV\nKtPpDgEkMfuZirl9H3E18uRSCvNwkdq9mzFTwFvulJ77Gc5kfORR3vmKIChMSLk/\nIFdyML9M7I0z7NVnw3p9Bl8C6eXzJtlbEx3CytTASoP0eHHdY/Uw8fVv+9JMglJ2\n7GTJJLDVYTjJFqJe8gwVQXHOB/MVfSI6p9vvt+PIb+A4poFqtATgLDFGq/a6VNmh\nvOVdReMosZq/3M11IqUqp28MfGMfhNXMP3jq4i4EkocAmKnfzaPOID3T0N2TMyHc\noVdTxTg7BApoVsBscze+pplaoYmTttrw/DEZ4RAwxF73vm0GKoMGf7dUXcuynLRd\n/QNy/UOUOi7xSVokNIRyZAa/0U32BTFTwl7VonhKxuZzKAJePGw3HWgx4uVFtl+o\nf4Z7a4qAmISl7hNvBlvG\n=69/f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-07T09:51:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url