owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/985b1e291418ef5ccdbdcf34c1e3edd3dcc1daa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:14:40Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T21:14:40Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"feat(ops): optional age encryption and retention pruning for module backups\n\n- SDKWORK_BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT encrypts every completed backup set to\n  .age objects on the target with checksums regenerated over the\n  ciphertext; a declared recipient without the age binary fails the\n  backup closed instead of silently shipping plaintext. All three\n  restore paths (config, database, volumes) decrypt host-side through\n  SDKWORK_BACKUP_AGE_IDENTITY_FILE, and verify works unchanged over the\n  ciphertext checksums. The manifest globs cover the encrypted artifacts.\n- sdkwork_backup_prune keeps the newest SDKWORK_BACKUP_KEEP sets per\n  environment (default 7) after a successful backup: names are\n  shape-checked (<module>-<environment>-<UTC stamp>) and removed one\n  explicit path at a time, with the sort/cut running on the target so\n  the operator workstation''s head need not be GNU.\n\nCalled from sdkwork-webserver''s backup runbook; retention documented\nthere alongside the encryption key-management instructions.","tree":{"sha":"efee4ed90e79cfec65c00a9b11fb8e087ab55e47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/efee4ed90e79cfec65c00a9b11fb8e087ab55e47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/985b1e291418ef5ccdbdcf34c1e3edd3dcc1daa3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.g