om/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/65a056ee0c309c65f0168c8db6ca46198fe37d8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:25:54Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:25:54Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"chore(gates): register check:client-host-packages as a guardrail\n\nThe host-package rule was executable since aa6e390 but registered nowhere, so\nnothing ran it against the fleet. That is the failure mode this registry exists\nto prevent: a normative clause with no gate behind it is how the workspace\naccumulated 1013 absolute path bindings without a single failure.\n\n  scope    repo      `--root {repo}`, matching the command the architecture\n                    standards publish in their verification tables\n  tier     guardrail known debt, must not grow\n  baseline 6         measured, not guessed\n\nMeasured with `node sdkwork-specs/tools/run-gate-matrix.mjs --only guardrail`\nagainst D:/sdkwork-space:\n\n  ok guardrail check:client-host-packages  exit=1  items=6  baseline=6  0s\n\nAll six items are real host-name defects, named in the entry''s note so the next\nround can drive the baseline to 0: sdkwork-appstore-pc-host and\nsdkwork-appstore-h5-host are generic architecture-free names, and\nsdkwork-autocut-desktop is not named after its sdkwork-video-cut-pc root. The\n11 migration-debt items (ten -pc-desktop aliases and the inert manifest on\nsdkwork-im-harmony-mobile-host) stay out of the baseline because debt is\nnon-fatal without --strict.\n\nRegistered through a synthetic blob built from HEAD, because this file carries\nanother session''s uncommitted rewrite of the workspace-path-portability note in\nthe same working tree. The commit therefore adds this one entry and nothing\nelse; that rewrite is still uncommitted and untouched, and the working-tree file\nwas written in place so the next `git add` of it cannot silently drop this entry.\n\nFour other guardrails are red in the same matrix run and none of them is\nattributable to this change - every finding is in another repository\n(sdkwork-knowledgebase topology, sdkwork-utils-kotlin gradlew placement,\na package.json that does not parse, and the portability scan). This commit\ntouches gates.manifest.json only.","tree":{"sha":"8140c5fd35269e0f255ba2f8002645c37bb65b8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/8140c5fd35269e0f255ba2f8002645c37bb65b8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/65a056ee0c309c65f0168c8db6ca46198fe37d8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/65a056ee0c309c65f0168c8db6ca46198fe37d8c","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKDY1YTA1NmVlMGMzMDljNjVmMDE2OGM4ZGI2Y2E0NjE5OGZlMzdkOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439","sha":"1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439"}],"sha":"65a056ee0c309c65f0168c8db6ca46198fe37d8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/65a056ee0c309c65f0168c8db6ca46198fe37d8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:19:19Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:19:19Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"docs(client-architecture): align the host-manifest prose with the gate\n\nFollow-up to aa6e390. The three verification rows the previous commit wrote\nstill told the reader a host package \"carries a `package.json`\", which is the\nrule that gate revision had just stopped enforcing, so the prose and the\nvalidator were pointing in opposite directions on the same line.\n\n- APP_PC_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC section 12 and DESKTOP_APP_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC: the\n  host package carries the manifest of its own ecosystem, listed per root kind,\n  and an inert `package.json` inside a native host package is migration debt.\n- APP_H5_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC section 15: the H5 root ecosystem manifest is\n  `package.json`, named as such rather than assumed.\n- HARMONY_APP_MOBILE_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC section 4: adds the rule itself, which\n  had no normative home. Every package carries `oh-package.json5` plus\n  `build-profile.json5`; a host package MUST NOT carry a `package.json`; the\n  `package.json` that check-frontend-composition reads as the composition\n  contract belongs to the core package only.\n\nTable integrity across the four files: 9 + 9 + 12 + 2 tables, 0 defects.\ntools/check-client-host-packages.test.mjs: 12/12.","tree":{"sha":"9a6991f74333c1eed46c79e692eb9573cac20ccd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/9a6991f74333c1eed46c79e692eb9573cac20ccd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKDFjMmNhNTViMGQyNGY3NDM1YzgwMDhjOTg2OTk3YTQ0YTFmOTY0Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e","sha":"aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e"}],"sha":"1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/1c2ca55b0d24f7435c8008c986997a44a1f96439"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:18:23Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:18:23Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"fix(specs): require each native host package''s own ecosystem manifest\n\nThe host-package gate required a `package.json` of every client-root host\npackage. That is wrong for every native root: each architecture spec already\nstates the package''s own manifest in its `Package Internal Shape` section.\n\n  harmony-mobile  oh-package.json5   HARMONY_APP_MOBILE_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC.md section 4\n  flutter-mobile  pubspec.yaml       FLUTTER_APP_MOBILE_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC.md\n  android-mobile  build.gradle.kts   ANDROID_APP_MOBILE_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC.md\n  ios-mobile      Package.swift      IOS_APP_MOBILE_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC.md\n\nSo the rule reported five false findings against the Harmony roots of\nsdkwork-agents, sdkwork-appstore, sdkwork-cloudrouter, sdkwork-knowledgebase\nand sdkwork-webserver, all of which carry `oh-package.json5` and no\n`package.json` at all. Workspace errors drop from 11 to 6; the 6 that remain\nare real (two generic host names, one host name missing its application code).\n\nAlso, a `package.json` inside a native host package is now reported as\nmigration debt. One exists, on sdkwork-im-harmony-mobile-host, marked with a\n`sdkwork.role` that no SDKWork standard defines and that no validator reads:\n`validateCoreCompositionLayout()` inspects the core package only, so the file\nis inert. Reported rather than deleted, because removing it is a separate\ndecision about that marker convention.\n\nSeparately, `--workspace` over a root that holds no governed repository now\nexits 2 instead of printing a clean run. A workspace root reached with a path\nthe shell did not translate used to pass silently; the gate is only a signal\nwhen it has something to scan.\n\nVerified: tools/check-client-host-packages.test.mjs 12/12 (was 9, added the\necosystem-manifest, inert-manifest and empty-workspace cases), and a full\nworkspace scan reports 6 errors / 11 debts against 30 host packages.","tree":{"sha":"a93ded10983746b9358327f07b5b1314f43c78be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/a93ded10983746b9358327f07b5b1314f43c78be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKGFhNmUzOTAzMzJmYWY4OWIyZjdlMGM4NjgzMWNhMGU0ZGIyZmUwNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4","sha":"0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4"}],"sha":"aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/aa6e390332faf89b2f7e0c86831ca0e4db2fe06e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:12:44Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T15:12:44Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"docs(client-architecture): close the PC/H5 native-host standards and add the host-package gate\n\nThe PC and H5 architecture standards already owned the Tauri, Electron, and\nCapacitor desktop hosts and the one H5 Capacitor mobile host, and the manifest\nvalidator already implemented the client-root-scoped rule. The prose had drifted\nfrom both the validator and real usage. This closes the drift and makes the rule\nexecutable.\n\nSpecification fixes:\n- APP_MANIFEST_SPEC: `clientArchitecture` host values are now resolved together\n  with the declaring client root and the entry `runtimeTarget`. The old text\n  claimed `capacitor` was valid only for `runtimeTarget = \"desktop\"`, which\n  contradicted `check-app-manifest-deployment-standard.mjs` (TARGET_RULES maps\n  `capacitor-ios` / `capacitor-android` to `capacitor`) and six real package\n  entries in sdkwork-birdcoder and sdkwork-birdcoder2 H5 roots. The H5 branch\n  now maps to `sdkwork-<application-code>-h5-capacitor`. The tablet row also\n  stopped excluding the `ios-native` / `android-native` values the validator\n  accepts.\n- APP_H5_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC: declares the Capacitor platform `clientArchitecture`\n  explicitly, normalizes the manifest-axis spelling to `runtimeTarget`, and\n  forbids a generic `-h5-host` package.\n- APP_PC_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC: documents the `-pc-desktop` -> `-pc-tauri` host\n  rename the migration alias requires, and fixes a pre-existing defect where a\n  nine-line prose block split the config-family table in two.\n- COMPONENT_SPEC: adds `electron-host`, `capacitor-host`, and `h5-capacitor-host`\n  component types, routes the PC and H5 host package roots to their architecture\n  standards, and stops the retired alias from being read as a capability package.\n- GITHUB_WORKFLOW_SPEC: desktop host architectures must be distinguished by\n  `targets[].variant` when one application ships more than one desktop host;\n  the packing formula carries a single `desktop` token, so Tauri and Electron\n  artifacts for the same platform would otherwise collide on one packageId.\n- DESKTOP_APP_ARCHITECTURE_SPEC: normalizes the manifest-axis spelling.\n- AGENTS.md and AGENTS_SPEC.md: route client-root and native-host work to the\n  matching architecture standards, which the task-type table previously omitted.\n\nNew gate:\n- tools/check-client-host-packages.mjs enforces architecture-explicit host names,\n  client-root ownership, one package per architecture, and package.json\n  presence. The retired `-pc-desktop` alias reports as migration debt and fails\n  under --strict. Verified against the workspace: 29 host packages across 16\n  client roots, 10 migration-debt items, 10 errors.\n- tools/check-client-host-packages.test.mjs covers nine cases.\n\nVerification: node --test tools/*.test.mjs -> 982 tests, 958 pass, 24 fail. All\n24 failures are pre-existing: a git-archive HEAD baseline fails the same suites\nand no suite that is red now is green at HEAD.","tree":{"sha":"1a9e356976d9df989aae3bc6fe2f90b9efccc253","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/1a9e356976d9df989aae3bc6fe2f90b9efccc253"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKDBiNjFiZWZkYTIxYTQwODc0ODliNGExNjljMDQxY2M1NGVjNTM5YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5","sha":"62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5"}],"sha":"0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/0b61befda21a4087489b4a169c041cc54ec539b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:41:25Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:41:25Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"docs(workspace): standardize opt-in standalone apps subtree repositories\n\n`apps/` is in-tree by default. A repository MAY instead own it as a\nstandalone `<application-code>-apps` sibling repository consumed as a git\nsubmodule, but only on an explicit per-repository owner instruction. The\nshape MUST NOT be changed by a template, generator, migration, alignment\npass, or automated sweep, and MUST NOT be inferred from repository size,\nclient-surface count, file count, or release cadence.\n\nAdds SDKWORK_WORKSPACE_SPEC.md section 1.1.4 covering both ownership\nshapes, the cross-reference from the apps/ definition in section 1.1, the\nmatching gitlink rule in section 6 (unlike `external/`, a standalone apps\nsubtree is SDKWork-owned source, so it is never shallow and never sets\nfetch.recurseSubmodules=false), four verification items in section 8, two\nacceptance-checklist entries in section 9, and the README spec index plus\na scenario-table entry so the option is discoverable.\n\nMotivation: letting one module''s client surfaces be developed, staffed,\npermissioned, and released on their own cadence when a separate team owns\nthem, without splitting the rest of the repository.\n\nIn-tree remains the baseline for onboarding and review; an apps/ gitlink\nis read as a deliberate, documented allocation decision.","tree":{"sha":"62834dfff68cacdf7100d78e1319a6aebd866a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/62834dfff68cacdf7100d78e1319a6aebd866a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKDYyZTZhNjU3NThmODg1Y2YzNGEwYTA3NjI2OTFiODcwZDJiODA4YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84","sha":"a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84"}],"sha":"62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/62e6a65758f885cf34a0a0762691b870d2b808b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:39:10Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:39:10Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"fix(database-framework): validate the bounded module roots under database/modules\n\nDATABASE_FRAMEWORK_SPEC.md section 5.3 lets an application root carry additional bounded database modules under database/modules/{module-id}/. Each one holds its own database.manifest.json, so each one is a module root in its own right and carries the required paths, engine directories, contract and seed manifest of its role. The gate validated only <root>/database, which reported the parent as clean while every bounded module went unread.\n\nThat is not hypothetical: five of cloudrouter''s seven bounded modules were missing required paths, one was missing its prefix and table registries, and payment-runtime''s baseline declares organization_id TEXT in eight places where DATABASE_SPEC DB089 requires NOT NULL DEFAULT ''0''. No gate said any of it, because no gate read those directories.\n\nDiscovery follows database.manifest.json rather than the directory name, so a scratch directory under modules/ is not mistaken for a module root, and it recurses because a bounded module may itself carry bounded modules. Both the layout and the contract checks run for a bounded root, and each failure is prefixed with the root it belongs to, so a reader can tell which of several roots is broken.\n\nMeasured before landing: 9 bounded roots across 2 repositories; appbase''s two pass unchanged, cloudrouter''s seven now report their real state. Across all 70 repositories the gate goes from 70/70 to 69/70, the single failure being cloudrouter''s payment-runtime, whose remaining gaps need an ownership decision.\n\nMutation-tested 4/4: unreachable discovery, unattributed failures, layout-only validation and manifest-blind discovery each turn the test red on the assertion that guards it.","tree":{"sha":"2620f4b81edabc5d6449fbe67f82c2bc47c7e50c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/2620f4b81edabc5d6449fbe67f82c2bc47c7e50c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKGE2MWJkMjM3MTdkODQ1MzhmMmExZDczNTc1M2M4YjUyZjQ2MTZhODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9","sha":"6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9"}],"sha":"a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/a61bd23717d84538f2a1d735753c8b52f4616a84"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:10:31Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:10:31Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"fix(provider-session-identity): exclude agent scratch from the scan\n\nThe walker keeps its own skip set and never listed .workbuddy, so an agent''s gate-health report - which by construction quotes the provider session terminology this check forbids - was counted as a product violation and pushed the repository one past its registered baseline. Added .workbuddy and __pycache__ alongside the existing .sdkwork/.tmp entries, matching the portability and shell-portability gates, which already treat .workbuddy as scratch.","tree":{"sha":"f32b9eacd5c2f4ce55aa41ad8729d2a87c0abdec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/f32b9eacd5c2f4ce55aa41ad8729d2a87c0abdec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKDZmYWY3N2IwOTU2YjIzZmUxYjBmMzFkMjMwYmMyZDg4NmVkYTFlZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/c072af71a47cefb8c24dd4e26b0ab2f6ca2db3a5","sha":"c072af71a47cefb8c24dd4e26b0ab2f6ca2db3a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/c072af71a47cefb8c24dd4e26b0ab2f6ca2db3a5"}],"sha":"6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/6faf77b0956b23fe1b0f31d230bc2d886eda1ee9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/c072af71a47cefb8c24dd4e26b0ab2f6ca2db3a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:02:35Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:02:35Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"chore(portability): checkpoint the portability gate, its suite and the path cleanup\n\nAdd tools/check-workspace-path-portability.mjs with its regression suite, register the\ngate in gates.manifest.json, expose pnpm test:workspace-path-portability, and extend\nDEPENDENCY_MANAGEMENT_SPEC.md plus PORTABILITY_SPEC.md section 5.2 to cover the\nline-scope and test-file exemption markers.\n\nThis working tree is shared with a concurrent session, so the checkpoint also captures\nthe in-flight PNPM_SCRIPT_SPEC.md work (with tools/check-pnpm-script-standard.mjs and\nits suite) and the tech-note reorganisation. It is a checkpoint for traceability, not a\nreviewed release.","tree":{"sha":"b153ed4314d25c4aa8f273aa40d53c99fa4b6f01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/trees/b153ed4314d25c4aa8f273aa40d53c99fa4b6f01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/git/commits/c072af71a47cefb8c24dd4e26b0ab2f6ca2db3a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQVw9w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/c072af71a47cefb8c24dd4e26b0ab2f6ca2db3a5","node_id":"C_kwDOSyFxZdoAKGMwNzJhZjcxYTQ3Y2VmYjhjMjRkZDRlMjZiMGFiMmY2Y2EyZGIzYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commit/1628990e4d0b9c1b8e502b94cfb0050310131152","sha":"1628990e4d0b9c1b8e502b94cfb0050310131152","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/1628990e4d0b9c1b8e502b94cfb0050310131152"}],"sha":"c072af71a47cefb8c24dd4e26b0ab2f6ca2db3a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-specs/commits/c072af71