l":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/YoungSella","id":155443947,"login":"YoungSella","node_id":"U_kgDOCUPi6w","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YoungSella","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/7233282f613e836058f4777040074a2e17bf223c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:19:51Z","email":"155443947+YoungSella@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YoungSella"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:19:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(docker): expose NEXT_PUBLIC_* as build args (#643)\n\nBrowser-side env vars must be baked at Next.js build time. Adding ARG/ENV pairs in the build stage allows operators to configure the gateway URL via docker build --build-arg or compose.yml args without forking the image. Backward-compatible: defaults remain empty, behaviour unchanged when no build args are passed. Discovered via Project EIGHTBALL deployment with separate subdomains for gateway and dashboard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniel Rose <sella-media-hq@Mac.fritz.box>","tree":{"sha":"74a2ed4a5dc004ce5bee81542e09fd7bbfa6754e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/trees/74a2ed4a5dc004ce5bee81542e09fd7bbfa6754e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/commits/7233282f613e836058f4777040074a2e17bf223c","verification":{"payload":"tree 74a2ed4a5dc004ce5bee81542e09fd7bbfa6754e\nparent 980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7\nauthor YoungSella <155443947+YoungSella@users.noreply.github.com> 1778127591 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778127591 +0700\n\nfeat(docker): expose NEXT_PUBLIC_* as build args (#643)\n\nBrowser-side env vars must be baked at Next.js build time. Adding ARG/ENV pairs in the build stage allows operators to configure the gateway URL via docker build --build-arg or compose.yml args without forking the image. Backward-compatible: defaults remain empty, behaviour unchanged when no build args are passed. Discovered via Project EIGHTBALL deployment with separate subdomains for gateway and dashboard.\n\nCo-authored-by: Daniel Rose <sella-media-hq@Mac.fritz.box>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BLnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9bkQAEhPimLS5F9g/us7eu/ChHs7\nVTCEqn8Qv2UD9WBezGgkumHnaHPg+XSuZefmVghL8F6oDTD67w9ULH7F8nuN/dyk\nEUcCvG6OAF2fJBPVrjXV6xCvQ3VziVjG8t1gLRDQgDcMBukCZ94dMccLZUtYg8EN\n3VfgvGKCWLLbN6zC5n7EwVpIZUvxw2M2KihFhf7TA6GxW8DVZn2pyPb9SYfOL/IQ\nfhfSs2N7Ir52jkK4/OWZO54LgSqVSvhCjRpnFBSwpQ/zAKaroTp0p5IZ18zbf28z\nGjN64R68q2SoUlfk+M3fbiy80KcfuCoo2Te5airXVdeofdvHze1P0l/UU+yfzPvt\nGixFEy72ztfnl8V/ErMYpbinF/YW1AxNDzAt8FaG+U8nR4S+ipU3vOQQco2WlsX8\nefh6rNGh/HsT64abuVSST9KDi9AzEKMcxWaj+V3eOhtf51f+UBHP3bJlF0M7VcwH\nrQDmeTH84ovuYCzu3RMLjEkc7it2vosifEMQAVrqOBZFHu0yPaHlqTM48q1eP8fI\ntrUh/YZyrwbrjGBZBxs9AxcJk4cquq+TQ3gApRZN0u8/oUvp5YatQAGCNS7rsgYd\nAmhpXvF1rk1a7qWja0/AvfZCx6G0kxue40hw0RMopPkO7lQpySp95U5A6YUKc07y\nP+V3PQ2EJEvrdFWS560T\n=GN6+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-05T16:11:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commit/7233282f613e836058f4777040074a2e17bf223c","node_id":"C_kwDOSyKZ_doAKDcyMzMyODJmNjEzZTgzNjA1OGY0Nzc3MDQwMDc0YTJlMTdiZjIyM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commit/980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7","sha":"980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7"}],"sha":"7233282f613e836058f4777040074a2e17bf223c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/7233282f613e836058f4777040074a2e17bf223c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21066097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nnnet","id":21066097,"login":"nnnet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY2MDk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:19:46Z","email":"zkowkmdx@sharklasers.com","name":"nnnet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:19:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(chat,csp): nonce hydration + chat session continuity with host Claude CLI (#647)\n\n## Summary\n\nFour small, independent bug fixes:\n\n1. **CSP nonce → next-themes hydration.** The CSP nonce was not forwarded to `next-themes`'' `ThemeProvider`, so theme hydration was blocked under our default CSP and the dashboard rendered with the wrong theme on the first paint. `src/proxy.ts` now propagates the nonce; `src/app/layout.tsx` consumes it.\n\n2. **`/api/sessions/continue` works on shared host Claude sessions.** When operators bind-mount their host `~/.claude/projects` into the container (a common pattern with the host-config projection in PR #646), the resolver couldn''t open sessions whose `.jsonl` lived under that mount. Path resolver now accepts both container-local and host-projected paths.\n\n3. **Tighter active-session window + drop orphan rows.** MC was treating any session whose `.jsonl` was touched recently as \"alive\" — even after the underlying Claude process had long stopped. The window is tighter now and orphan rows are filtered.\n\n4. **Chat input stays anchored.** The chat input lost focus on every message because the whole transcript re-rendered. We anchor the input and patch the transcript instead.\n\n## Why this is useful upstream\n\nThese are user-visible defects that anyone running MC behind a CSP or sharing host Claude state hits within minutes of using the chat panel. None depend on each other or on any other in-flight PR.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Visit the dashboard with a strict CSP — theme matches the user''s preference on first paint, no hydration errors in console.\n- Bind-mount host `~/.claude/projects` into the dev container, open a session that exists only on the host — `/api/sessions/continue` resolves it.\n- Watch `/api/sessions` after killing a Claude process — the orphan row disappears within the new window.\n- Send several chat messages — input keeps focus across each reply.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSquashes our fork''s commits:\n- `9ac39a6 fix(csp): pass nonce to next-themes ThemeProvider so hydration works`\n- `d7c10b2 fix(chat): /api/sessions/continue works on shared host claude sessions`\n- `8463a70 fix(chat): tighter active-session window + remove orphan rows`\n- `2fce07a fix(chat): keep input anchored, reply renders into transcript`","tree":{"sha":"47464011cc0737e32f0964c4bbaf5eb87564ba35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/trees/47464011cc0737e32f0964c4bbaf5eb87564ba35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/commits/980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7","verification":{"payload":"tree 47464011cc0737e32f0964c4bbaf5eb87564ba35\nparent 7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5\nauthor nnnet <zkowkmdx@sharklasers.com> 1778127586 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778127586 +0700\n\nfix(chat,csp): nonce hydration + chat session continuity with host Claude CLI (#647)\n\n## Summary\n\nFour small, independent bug fixes:\n\n1. **CSP nonce → next-themes hydration.** The CSP nonce was not forwarded to `next-themes`'' `ThemeProvider`, so theme hydration was blocked under our default CSP and the dashboard rendered with the wrong theme on the first paint. `src/proxy.ts` now propagates the nonce; `src/app/layout.tsx` consumes it.\n\n2. **`/api/sessions/continue` works on shared host Claude sessions.** When operators bind-mount their host `~/.claude/projects` into the container (a common pattern with the host-config projection in PR #646), the resolver couldn''t open sessions whose `.jsonl` lived under that mount. Path resolver now accepts both container-local and host-projected paths.\n\n3. **Tighter active-session window + drop orphan rows.** MC was treating any session whose `.jsonl` was touched recently as \"alive\" — even after the underlying Claude process had long stopped. The window is tighter now and orphan rows are filtered.\n\n4. **Chat input stays anchored.** The chat input lost focus on every message because the whole transcript re-rendered. We anchor the input and patch the transcript instead.\n\n## Why this is useful upstream\n\nThese are user-visible defects that anyone running MC behind a CSP or sharing host Claude state hits within minutes of using the chat panel. None depend on each other or on any other in-flight PR.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Visit the dashboard with a strict CSP — theme matches the user''s preference on first paint, no hydration errors in console.\n- Bind-mount host `~/.claude/projects` into the dev container, open a session that exists only on the host — `/api/sessions/continue` resolves it.\n- Watch `/api/sessions` after killing a Claude process — the orphan row disappears within the new window.\n- Send several chat messages — input keeps focus across each reply.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSquashes our fork''s commits:\n- `9ac39a6 fix(csp): pass nonce to next-themes ThemeProvider so hydration works`\n- `d7c10b2 fix(chat): /api/sessions/continue works on shared host claude sessions`\n- `8463a70 fix(chat): tighter active-session window + remove orphan rows`\n- `2fce07a fix(chat): keep input anchored, reply renders into transcript`","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BLiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG2kQAK2dTzGEPZFPsy0h8QhThP2b\n4maGLquInl0BbsoSooDZyOWHfnNACZZJDWmkXBBvV8cG+ofkAhy1p4fiOW3M6eyB\nbTHspza57LMzzV6Z19kWugGL5gMdVbsENqRD6zRHD678hJ8p+h+Ao0Pol/v0A6+W\n3Qw2XF8yhZnLGp47A0f+aki0La/m9vf7KSDP75q7K4lbncOmA1hy+rh5To95CXFz\n4lWrHHgu3NQjQe7vTEA/JgSuBHcmi1ceF6Kcl9G/JC6365rX7/2HHR5rKuy5eE3Y\n2nxucn6Kz/HUJ1rm0oVFHjDop+jYI2KX5Zw7CPNY8QfiTK+VExf+SSoRJRKMNlnC\nNWLJSlvmVCWPFrIO24aIxDmkdSu6t2vphcQhnDjY4QVVrJsAjiiTxAN0pPKsVKH2\nywEMRJgzQ28p2WVIcO5wp3PZrQ6LrHSZzb9xKiMRLKaH2s65Lj3bpF4CmhOp9Awc\nX+VrP+356eSpCGEEMgYOFShTM//FjsMhxCsZnu1+V+qh5B1Xem+3sP5RNZZ3aKAA\nIn/Fly0yrQNqDhTrNUEq2bKMCMyeRPeQT8rlGsAMpsNO2IKP0IkOaK6SVeIbDTSO\naIk0QAwNV/KkclUco1brzL0sbLbvw17BXELoPS5tUP9aXYf9Csy8kYXmR5UnlNLS\nmM1Wd1N6hOE2ohKY7q/L\n=RNNx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-05T16:11:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commit/980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7","node_id":"C_kwDOSyKZ_doAKDk4MGFlODQ0OTQxNDk5MGUwM2E0ZmIxNjQ2ODRlZDIzZWNiYmJhYzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commit/7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5","sha":"7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5"}],"sha":"980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/980ae8449414990e03a4fb164684ed23ecbbbac7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21066097?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/nnnet","id":21066097,"login":"nnnet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY2MDk3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nnnet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:15:20Z","email":"zkowkmdx@sharklasers.com","name":"nnnet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:15:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(dispatch): direct multi-provider dispatch (Anthropic / OpenAI / local OpenAI-compatible) (#648)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a direct-dispatch path for tasks so MC no longer requires the OpenClaw gateway to reach LLMs. When the gateway isn''t available — most commonly on Linux deployments where the macOS-native gateway can''t be installed — MC now calls provider HTTP APIs itself.\n\n### Supported direct providers\n\n| Provider | Env variable | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Anthropic** | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Smart Opus/Sonnet/Haiku selection via `classifyDirectModel()` heuristics. |\n| **OpenAI** | `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Models like `openai/gpt-4o-mini`, `openai/gpt-5-nano` selectable per-agent. |\n| **Any OpenAI-compatible local** | `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT`, optional `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` | LMStudio, Ollama, vLLM — anything serving `/v1/chat/completions`. |\n\nEach agent''s `agent_config.dispatchModel` overrides the heuristics (e.g. set `openai/gpt-4o-mini` to lock that agent to OpenAI).\n\n### Hardened gateway-availability check\n\n`isGatewayAvailable()` previously returned `true` whenever `~/.openclaw` was a non-empty path string — which is the **default** even when OpenClaw isn''t installed. On Linux this caused `useDirectApi = !true && … = false`, so MC fell through to `runOpenClaw(...)` and crashed with `spawn openclaw ENOENT`.\n\nThe check now requires physical evidence:\n- A real `openclaw.json` exists at `config.openclawConfigPath`, **or**\n- A `gateways` row whose status is in `{online, healthy, ready}` (the seed `unknown` row planted by onboarding doesn''t count).\n\n## Why this is useful upstream\n\nDropping the macOS-only constraint is the single biggest barrier to running MC in cloud / Linux dev environments. With this change, an operator can `git clone`, set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, and dispatch tasks immediately — no gateway, no Mac, no extra processes.\n\n## Walkthrough\n\n`examples/MULTI-PROVIDER-DEMO.md` is a field-by-field walkthrough that builds a three-agent team using all three direct providers (Anthropic for the lead, OpenAI for the worker, local LMStudio for the reviewer) and runs an end-to-end task.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Run on a Linux host with no OpenClaw installed; confirm `/agents` shows \"No gateways installed\" and dispatch still works.\n- Set only `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and dispatch a task — logs show \"Dispatching task via direct Claude API\".\n- Set only `OPENAI_API_KEY`, set agent `dispatchModel: openai/gpt-4o-mini`, dispatch — logs show OpenAI direct.\n- Bring up LMStudio at `127.0.0.1:1234`, set `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1`, dispatch with `dispatchModel: local/<your-model>` — logs show local direct.\n- With OpenClaw running and a healthy `gateways` row, dispatch — `useDirectApi=false`, gateway path used as before. Backwards-compatible.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSquashes:\n- `70328ad feat(dispatch): direct OpenAI + OpenAI-compatible local providers`\n- `762ed51 fix(dispatch): make MC self-sufficient without OpenClaw gateway`\n- `8def310 docs(deployment): document host-config projection, direct providers, host session modes`\n- `bdd86ea docs(examples): add multi-provider team walkthrough`\n- `c7627c7 docs(examples): expand multi-provider demo into a field-by-field walkthrough`","tree":{"sha":"600bc09b83014af9f10f3ebcfa355ff559d64ea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/trees/600bc09b83014af9f10f3ebcfa355ff559d64ea7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/commits/7ba23867032607a7c02ed927e9c493eaf68b0cb5","verification":{"payload":"tree 600bc09b83014af9f10f3ebcfa355ff559d64ea7\nparent b92c23a2e67789343514f5bc80aa19f6e5bb6bed\nauthor nnnet <zkowkmdx@sharklasers.com> 1778127320 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778127320 +0700\n\nfeat(dispatch): direct multi-provider dispatch (Anthropic / OpenAI / local OpenAI-compatible) (#648)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a direct-dispatch path for tasks so MC no longer requires the OpenClaw gateway to reach LLMs. When the gateway isn''t available — most commonly on Linux deployments where the macOS-native gateway can''t be installed — MC now calls provider HTTP APIs itself.\n\n### Supported direct providers\n\n| Provider | Env variable | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Anthropic** | `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | Smart Opus/Sonnet/Haiku selection via `classifyDirectModel()` heuristics. |\n| **OpenAI** | `OPENAI_API_KEY` | Models like `openai/gpt-4o-mini`, `openai/gpt-5-nano` selectable per-agent. |\n| **Any OpenAI-compatible local** | `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT`, optional `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY` | LMStudio, Ollama, vLLM — anything serving `/v1/chat/completions`. |\n\nEach agent''s `agent_config.dispatchModel` overrides the heuristics (e.g. set `openai/gpt-4o-mini` to lock that agent to OpenAI).\n\n### Hardened gateway-availability check\n\n`isGatewayAvailable()` previously returned `true` whenever `~/.openclaw` was a non-empty path string — which is the **default** even when OpenClaw isn''t installed. On Linux this caused `useDirectApi = !true && … = false`, so MC fell through to `runOpenClaw(...)` and crashed with `spawn openclaw ENOENT`.\n\nThe check now requires physical evidence:\n- A real `openclaw.json` exists at `config.openclawConfigPath`, **or**\n- A `gateways` row whose status is in `{online, healthy, ready}` (the seed `unknown` row planted by onboarding doesn''t count).\n\n## Why this is useful upstream\n\nDropping the macOS-only constraint is the single biggest barrier to running MC in cloud / Linux dev environments. With this change, an operator can `git clone`, set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, and dispatch tasks immediately — no gateway, no Mac, no extra processes.\n\n## Walkthrough\n\n`examples/MULTI-PROVIDER-DEMO.md` is a field-by-field walkthrough that builds a three-agent team using all three direct providers (Anthropic for the lead, OpenAI for the worker, local LMStudio for the reviewer) and runs an end-to-end task.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Run on a Linux host with no OpenClaw installed; confirm `/agents` shows \"No gateways installed\" and dispatch still works.\n- Set only `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and dispatch a task — logs show \"Dispatching task via direct Claude API\".\n- Set only `OPENAI_API_KEY`, set agent `dispatchModel: openai/gpt-4o-mini`, dispatch — logs show OpenAI direct.\n- Bring up LMStudio at `127.0.0.1:1234`, set `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1`, dispatch with `dispatchModel: local/<your-model>` — logs show local direct.\n- With OpenClaw running and a healthy `gateways` row, dispatch — `useDirectApi=false`, gateway path used as before. Backwards-compatible.\n\n## Provenance\n\nSquashes:\n- `70328ad feat(dispatch): direct OpenAI + OpenAI-compatible local providers`\n- `762ed51 fix(dispatch): make MC self-sufficient without OpenClaw gateway`\n- `8def310 docs(deployment): document host-config projection, direct providers, host session modes`\n- `bdd86ea docs(examples): add multi-provider team walkthrough`\n- `c7627c7 docs(examples): expand multi-provider demo into a field-by-field walkthrough`","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BHYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbB0QAGJWuiFnzKN13Dotfs3Gziqa\nSYpPll3QHlnLAAHRx9XuiRZXJDegg49xPaX41+NdJxmPIAzx8HmibjRm4nHqu178\nTpRCztankXXUUFGkmSKrr/XabeLm2Gf6DI0PWC1ymksCHK55CqvMzuxM5c/HrU0q\n6zhZQ1xsa+9G53SsUpq8ApruhvRTpSHR/lbd9OBHWHdooaau0OkjLLmGwYFfv6Ac\nx1jIHMR2lupX+JoSjpBY4csqJTn63XT9JBgqVN2ufn5zkHDvpAbI/iM+iDcjLmr2\naMYD40v70Yxks8t+C1IoWJ6sQdHKMtM3uDTVFII6EIUE6k9yfWpUhWIyTf7Tq6s9\nmDZ4M8rOSt6eTJWhNiz8NmN8HR8amqb6Xs4eFltiaWPY8McYHa9AQv7Yl8pHTwx4\ny+opflSFqTRRij2icgjwkXw6+S2BdHkWEJhG7XvzJxyDio6h1Sj4jKMIGNZ+rUTg\nPkRhvTnN6caqozd7OZSXMiU+JhWuq8gSdMVgI28nF9BPGiIfynYJsjzuCVhgaLgL\naIDSpGDsP08eXOiTRopf3hnJIYreSrpgv1N0vBzDGjHLraSGBkSKZi1Wmfmo03DV\nphTaCAmKrifg/+vjPbp9t5QmTvMVrb1pprQ7/A7RtXOFT3nQDa8VAGjE1rgcE2gY\nGNN8gaMC9kxesZBaaHX8\n=USv/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-05T16:11:58Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}",