tps://api.github.com/users/codingDr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/codingDr","id":18496633,"login":"codingDr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDk2NjMz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codingDr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/commits/3c8ef6e5d8909f77b18175e7e7cfec7c6b40c780/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:10:19Z","email":"18496633+codingDr@users.noreply.github.com","name":"codingDr"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-07T04:10:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(agents): flatten gateway_config into buildAgentConfig overrides (#601)\n\nbuildAgentConfig expects a flat overrides shape, but the POST /api/agents\ntemplate branch was passing the nested gateway_config object with `as any`.\nThat silenced a real mismatch: overrides.model was {primary: \"<id>\"}, and\nthe function assigned the whole object to config.model.primary. Agents\ncreated from a template got a doubly-wrapped primary in the DB, crashing\nthe Models and Config tabs with \"Objects are not valid as a React child\n(found: object with keys {primary})\".\n\nExtract the leaf fields at the call site so the primary string survives\nand the other template overrides (identity, sandbox, subagents) actually\napply. Unit test locks in that overrides.model yields a string primary.\n\nFixes #599","tree":{"sha":"9a726f26bd75df5eed2ed2c28ae8951179445297","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/trees/9a726f26bd75df5eed2ed2c28ae8951179445297"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/governancemanners-coder/mission-control/git/commits/3c8ef6e5d8909f77b18175e7e7cfec7c6b40c780","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a726f26bd75df5eed2ed2c28ae8951179445297\nparent 549190576bcc08e4a7d2edc6e7839e5ca32efd15\nauthor codingDr <18496633+codingDr@users.noreply.github.com> 1778127019 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778127019 +0700\n\nfix(agents): flatten gateway_config into buildAgentConfig overrides (#601)\n\nbuildAgentConfig expects a flat overrides shape, but the POST /api/agents\ntemplate branch was passing the nested gateway_config object with `as any`.\nThat silenced a real mismatch: overrides.model was {primary: \"<id>\"}, and\nthe function assigned the whole object to config.model.primary. Agents\ncreated from a template got a doubly-wrapped primary in the DB, crashing\nthe Models and Config tabs with \"Objects are not valid as a React child\n(found: object with keys {primary})\".\n\nExtract the leaf fields at the call site so the primary string survives\nand the other template overrides (identity, sandbox, subagents) actually\napply. Unit test locks in that overrides.model yields a string primary.\n\nFixes #599","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/BCrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGe8QAKTuY3E6HeLVHwUfscb/5/Oy\nfT4xfhQjKkAhTD3S1dhySJdkuPDqROozH1mfWNWT1jfqoS8xJ0LzaVDsSKVOxvnV\naqdcg61YSgMMK/gNp7Neo1wMB5+zmdSYp/Inx0WpcinH3mguyugI6m1EAapZOvix\nz6ljRpCa9t4r2suRWDw+sGXy8dLlq/xk1Ywv2Sgv9Y6HNbf382hYCuCLsEfLxuSP\ntctws/43yJLzt8/j4UWKQ7NSGosSNMzK9fcOl3KdjHFoHmMvhHx7lrAhRNfrtDvB\nOD77RWDyV2M9EjY7LTOsXwZBzcgoaDSmfwc8z4XTZqym1d4a+kRFy64MwN0ZNopM\n2Ha/qD9zglKUsaNfbOWaiiStPztPp0AUaU45Mv0NP4kzWyht4dnOMGHf1NX0bLo2\nEP6XcUHGFL53EHg2dyMWOaCvcrMJPnegkM+BbHSI7n7/AZArj/td61ojkCuy